WEBVTT

01:42.811 --> 01:44.605
All the food's gonna go bad.

01:47.107 --> 01:48.692
Yeah, I drew up a list.

01:48.775 --> 01:51.904
I'll hit the store before
it gets all bought out.

01:54.031 --> 01:55.240
Fuck.

01:55.324 --> 01:56.450
Can you save it?

01:56.533 --> 01:57.784
No, no way.

01:57.868 --> 02:00.454
No, I gotta start over from scratch.

02:00.537 --> 02:02.956
I'll call the studio when
the phones get back up,

02:03.040 --> 02:04.499
see if they can extend my deadline.

02:05.709 --> 02:07.377
What choice do they have?

02:10.589 --> 02:14.134
You kiddin'? They could whip up
some bad Photoshop poster in an afternoon.

02:14.218 --> 02:16.094
They do it all the time, two big heads.

02:16.178 --> 02:18.222
I should've brought it downstairs
with me last night,

02:18.305 --> 02:20.057
I was just stupid, I guess.

02:20.140 --> 02:22.226
Well, sweetie, you couldn't exactly know

02:22.309 --> 02:24.311
that a tree was gonna come
flying through the window.

02:24.394 --> 02:27.147
Yeah, I'll hit the hardware store too,
get some plastic sheeting and duct tape

02:27.231 --> 02:29.399
and seal this up before
it gets dark, you know.

02:29.483 --> 02:31.235
Order in some new glass.

02:32.611 --> 02:34.112
Aw, you know what?

02:34.196 --> 02:36.823
That was your grandfather's tree,
the one he planted.

02:37.741 --> 02:39.409
I used to play in that tree.

02:39.493 --> 02:40.661
It's just stuff though.

02:40.744 --> 02:43.163
You know, we're safe,
that's all that counts.

02:43.247 --> 02:44.831
Yeah.

02:44.915 --> 02:46.208
Mom, Dad, you gotta come see!

02:46.291 --> 02:47.834
Hey, Billy, take it easy, all right?

02:47.918 --> 02:49.670
I really don't want you
running all over the place.

02:49.753 --> 02:50.796
But you gotta come look!

02:50.879 --> 02:52.172
The boathouse is all bashed.

02:52.256 --> 02:53.340
Holy crap!

02:53.840 --> 02:54.967
Billy!

02:55.050 --> 02:57.761
Sorry, Mom,
but you just gotta come, come on.

03:02.349 --> 03:03.392
Come on!

03:03.475 --> 03:05.769
Having spoken, the Doomsayer departs.

03:07.896 --> 03:10.315
How do you two always manage
to make me laugh?

03:10.857 --> 03:13.026
You have incredibly low standards.

03:13.735 --> 03:16.822
All right, let's go see the damage.

03:16.905 --> 03:17.906
No!

03:23.036 --> 03:25.080
- Norton's tree.
- Yeah.

03:26.707 --> 03:28.333
You mean the dead one I've been asking him

03:28.417 --> 03:30.669
to take down for three years
before it finally blew over?

03:30.752 --> 03:31.753
That tree?

03:32.713 --> 03:34.256
It really got smooshed.

03:34.756 --> 03:36.133
You ain't kiddin'.

03:37.509 --> 03:38.844
Look at that.

03:41.054 --> 03:42.639
What is it, Daddy?

03:43.932 --> 03:44.933
Mist?

03:45.892 --> 03:48.729
- On the lake?
- We've had mist on the lake before.

03:49.354 --> 03:50.981
Coming off the mountain like that?

03:51.064 --> 03:54.484
Two fronts meeting,
leftover from the storm?

03:54.568 --> 03:56.153
Something like that?

03:56.236 --> 03:58.947
- You sure?
- Honey, I'm not the weatherman.

03:59.031 --> 04:02.492
Why don't you take Billy, get him dressed?
I'll take him to town with me.

04:02.576 --> 04:04.369
All right. Where you goin'?

04:04.453 --> 04:06.913
I'm gonna go have a little chat
with our neighbor about his tree.

04:06.997 --> 04:08.081
Hon.

04:08.165 --> 04:10.417
Don't worry, I'm not gonna
punch him in the nose.

04:10.500 --> 04:11.543
You know what he's gonna say.

04:11.626 --> 04:14.671
He's gonna say "Sue me,"
which, I don't know, maybe we should.

04:14.755 --> 04:19.259
Honey, one property dispute with this guy
is enough to last me a lifetime.

04:19.343 --> 04:22.095
I'm gonna ask for
his insurance information.

04:22.179 --> 04:24.097
- Okay.
- That's all.

04:24.181 --> 04:25.432
Yeah.

04:29.144 --> 04:30.771
Motherfucker!

04:33.523 --> 04:35.067
Aw, shit!

04:35.734 --> 04:37.819
You motherfucker!

04:38.695 --> 04:39.946
Cocksucker!

04:42.074 --> 04:43.241
"Turn on,

04:43.742 --> 04:44.993
full choke,

04:45.660 --> 04:46.953
pull five,

04:47.037 --> 04:48.163
choke."

04:52.125 --> 04:53.877
I guess you've seen the...

04:55.170 --> 04:56.296
Boathouse.

04:56.380 --> 04:57.672
Yeah, and?

04:57.756 --> 04:58.924
Nothin'.

04:59.466 --> 05:02.636
Just think we should trade insurance info,
you know?

05:02.719 --> 05:03.804
That's all.

05:06.765 --> 05:08.975
My insurance guy's gonna love me.

05:13.230 --> 05:14.272
Shit.

05:14.356 --> 05:15.774
The 1980.

05:15.857 --> 05:19.236
I was gonna bring the station wagon,
but, I don't know,

05:19.319 --> 05:21.571
the weather was so beautiful
coming out of New York, I just...

05:21.655 --> 05:22.697
You know, top down.

05:22.781 --> 05:24.574
I'm sorry, man, I mean it.

05:24.658 --> 05:25.909
Sincerely.

05:27.661 --> 05:29.037
That's nice of you to say.

05:29.121 --> 05:32.249
No, that car was cherry.
I hate to see it like that.

05:35.627 --> 05:36.711
Okay, I'll tell you what.

05:36.795 --> 05:39.506
I'll find my insurance guy's number,
I'll bring it by later.

05:39.589 --> 05:41.425
- Is that okay?
- No problem.

05:47.347 --> 05:48.598
So, David.

05:50.892 --> 05:54.312
You're not heading into town
today by any chance, are you?

06:08.743 --> 06:10.912
Well, CMP's out in force.

06:11.746 --> 06:14.833
- Maybe we'll get our power back.
- That was some storm, huh?

06:14.916 --> 06:16.668
One for the books, yeah.

06:16.751 --> 06:18.295
For a moment there last night

06:18.378 --> 06:20.464
I thought we were gonna
take off and head for Oz.

06:21.173 --> 06:25.343
WZON is off the air,
but Portland's still broadcasting.

06:25.427 --> 06:26.553
Daddy, look!

06:28.221 --> 06:29.764
Guys from the base.

06:29.848 --> 06:31.975
From up the mountain?

06:32.058 --> 06:33.602
The Arrowhead Project?

06:34.853 --> 06:36.396
Well, you're a local.

06:36.480 --> 06:38.148
Any idea what they do up there?

06:38.231 --> 06:39.941
Missile defense research, you know,

06:40.025 --> 06:42.027
I'm sure you've heard the stories.

06:42.110 --> 06:44.112
Sure. The woman at the Laundromat says

06:44.196 --> 06:48.074
that they have a crashed flying saucer
up there with frozen alien bodies.

06:48.158 --> 06:49.910
Right, Miss Edna, yeah.

06:49.993 --> 06:51.203
Miss Tabloid.

06:52.787 --> 06:55.373
"I Had Bigfoot's Baby."

06:56.583 --> 06:59.044
"Satan's Face Appears in Oil Well Fire."

06:59.127 --> 07:00.921
You know, real reliable stuff.

07:05.258 --> 07:06.676
They're in a hurry.

07:06.760 --> 07:08.595
Maybe their power's out too.

07:17.979 --> 07:19.314
Still no signal.

07:19.856 --> 07:21.983
Why don't you go ahead?
I'm gonna try Steff on the pay phone.

07:22.067 --> 07:23.985
Can I go with Mr. Norton, Daddy?

07:24.069 --> 07:26.738
Sure, if you promise
to hold his hand, I guess.

07:26.821 --> 07:28.532
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

07:28.615 --> 07:29.866
Here's a list.

07:29.950 --> 07:31.159
- Okay.
- Okay?

07:31.243 --> 07:32.494
Meet you guys in there.

07:34.120 --> 07:35.288
Hold hands.

07:38.917 --> 07:41.378
I'm sorry,
I didn't know it was your sister.

07:45.674 --> 07:47.676
...looks so freaky.

07:57.102 --> 07:59.938
- Sally, hey. You guys look jammed up.
- Hey, Mr. Drayton.

08:00.021 --> 08:03.108
Yeah, well, half the staff didn't show,
plus the power's out.

08:03.191 --> 08:05.819
Oh, no. What, no backup generator?

08:05.902 --> 08:07.195
Only to keep the food cold.

08:07.279 --> 08:09.948
Everything else, welcome to the Dark Ages
and bring your checkbook.

08:10.031 --> 08:12.826
Hey, Thursday night,
Steff and I want a date night.

08:12.909 --> 08:15.036
- Babysit?
- Heck yeah, I'm there.

08:16.496 --> 08:17.831
Oh, my God.

08:17.914 --> 08:19.249
The storm.

08:19.332 --> 08:22.419
Everybody's stocking up,
been like this since we opened.

08:22.502 --> 08:23.795
Crappy day, huh?

08:23.878 --> 08:26.548
Everyone's a little pissed off
this morning.

08:26.631 --> 08:29.009
Morning, Mrs. Carmody.

08:29.092 --> 08:31.553
With lines like these,
I don't know how good it is,

08:31.636 --> 08:34.723
but I guess we'll have to make do.

08:34.806 --> 08:36.474
Keep your head down, pal.

08:36.558 --> 08:37.559
I know it.

08:41.104 --> 08:42.188
Hey, champ.

08:43.481 --> 08:45.108
Your wife should be a doctor.

08:45.191 --> 08:47.277
She could make a fortune in Manhattan
with this handwriting.

08:47.360 --> 08:49.571
Yeah, it takes some getting used to.

08:50.071 --> 08:52.365
Why don't you get your stuff?
I'll meet you at the checkout.

08:52.449 --> 08:53.533
Okay, done.

08:55.952 --> 08:57.495
Hey, David.

08:57.579 --> 08:59.122
Thanks for helping me out today.

09:02.876 --> 09:05.295
Are you and Mr. Norton
gonna be friends now, Daddy?

09:05.378 --> 09:06.963
I don't know.

09:07.964 --> 09:09.883
Friends might be stretching it a little.

09:10.884 --> 09:13.261
Guess you're not mad
at each other anymore.

09:13.345 --> 09:14.888
I guess not.

09:14.971 --> 09:17.891
Hey, and that's a start, eh?

09:18.808 --> 09:20.977
I'm sorry, ma'am, the register's down.

09:21.061 --> 09:22.979
The power outage got us too.

09:23.063 --> 09:25.607
Hopefully we'll have power up pretty soon.

09:25.690 --> 09:28.735
I asked.
I asked for just a little something.

09:35.450 --> 09:37.035
The bus leaves in 30 minutes.

09:37.118 --> 09:38.286
We'll make it, okay?

09:38.370 --> 09:40.789
You guys get the goodies,
I'll wait in line.

09:45.710 --> 09:48.171
I need some change on register 5.

09:49.214 --> 09:51.132
Good morning, Ms. Reppler.

09:51.216 --> 09:52.759
Hello, Ms. Reppler.

09:52.842 --> 09:55.762
Well, hello to you, Billy Drayton.

09:55.845 --> 09:57.472
How'd you hold up in the storm?

09:57.555 --> 09:59.766
We had a tree come through
the picture window last night,

09:59.849 --> 10:01.017
right in my studio.

10:01.101 --> 10:02.811
And the boathouse got all smooshed.

10:02.894 --> 10:04.312
Mr. Norton's tree fell on it.

10:04.396 --> 10:06.314
Ouch.

10:06.398 --> 10:07.941
Sorry to hear that.

10:10.694 --> 10:12.237
Well, how'd you guys make out?

10:12.320 --> 10:13.655
We're fine.

10:13.738 --> 10:15.156
It's the listings I'm worried about.

10:15.240 --> 10:18.201
At the very least, I'll bet every one
of our "For Sale" signs fell over.

10:18.284 --> 10:21.037
We had damage at the school,
wouldn't you know?

10:21.121 --> 10:23.873
That's what we get for
not fixing that roof when we should've.

10:23.957 --> 10:27.252
But with funds being cut every year,

10:27.335 --> 10:29.295
you'd think educating children

10:29.379 --> 10:31.381
would be more of a priority
in this country,

10:31.464 --> 10:33.133
but you'd be wrong.

10:33.633 --> 10:36.511
Government's got better things
to spend our money on,

10:36.594 --> 10:40.390
like corporate handouts
and building bombs.

10:53.987 --> 10:55.822
Daddy, is there a fire?
Is Mommy all right?

10:55.905 --> 10:58.366
I'm sure she's fine. Don't worry, okay?

10:59.784 --> 11:01.828
Mind what you're doing, Sally.

11:01.911 --> 11:04.622
Come on, we've got 10 days leave.
Check our papers.

11:04.706 --> 11:08.084
Look, I told you, all leaves are canceled.
I don't know why.

11:08.168 --> 11:09.794
I gotta go check the pharmacy out.

11:09.878 --> 11:12.547
Three men meet me back
at the jeep in 5 minutes.

11:12.630 --> 11:13.798
That's an order.

11:16.050 --> 11:17.802
Shit, man.

11:17.886 --> 11:20.013
Another half an hour, we'd have been gone.

11:52.712 --> 11:54.255
Oh, my God.

12:02.096 --> 12:03.973
Something in the mist!

12:04.891 --> 12:07.727
Something in the mist took John Lee!

12:07.811 --> 12:09.187
Dan, catch your breath!

12:09.270 --> 12:10.814
Something in the mist took John Lee.

12:10.897 --> 12:12.649
I could hear him screaming.

12:13.233 --> 12:15.652
Shut the doors! Shut the doors, my God!

12:15.735 --> 12:17.946
Daddy, I'm scared. Can we go home?

12:21.991 --> 12:23.368
Don't go out there.

12:23.451 --> 12:25.578
There's something in the mist.
It took John Lee!

12:25.662 --> 12:27.747
Screw that, I'm getting in my car.

12:27.831 --> 12:29.249
Mister, no!

13:01.614 --> 13:03.116
Please hold me.

13:03.992 --> 13:05.201
It's okay, it's okay.

13:05.285 --> 13:06.995
It's a pollution cloud,

13:07.078 --> 13:09.831
from the mills, down in Rumsford.

13:09.914 --> 13:12.584
Some kind of chemical explosion,
has to be.

13:14.752 --> 13:16.045
What is it?

13:17.005 --> 13:18.298
What's going on?

13:21.384 --> 13:22.468
It's death.

13:22.468 --> 13:52.468
Subtitle | www.movieddl.me

14:01.049 --> 14:02.091
Daddy!

14:21.235 --> 14:22.946
That was an earthquake.

14:23.655 --> 14:26.532
I tell ya, the goddamn mills blew up!

14:26.616 --> 14:28.076
Is everyone okay?

14:28.159 --> 14:29.577
Is anyone hurt?

14:29.661 --> 14:31.120
Everybody just stay put, okay?

14:31.204 --> 14:32.956
Just stay inside the store.

14:33.039 --> 14:34.415
I can't.

14:34.499 --> 14:36.167
I can't stay here.
I gotta get home to my kids.

14:36.250 --> 14:39.045
No, no, don't go out there.

14:39.128 --> 14:41.923
It's death out there.
It's the end of days.

14:42.006 --> 14:44.467
Stop it, okay? Stop it.

14:44.550 --> 14:47.428
Please, everybody,
everybody just relax. Okay?

14:47.512 --> 14:48.972
He's right. Let's just stay cool.

14:49.055 --> 14:50.473
Let's just try to figure out
what happened.

14:50.556 --> 14:51.724
I'm sorry.

14:51.808 --> 14:54.811
I can't just stay here.
I have to get home to my kids.

14:54.894 --> 14:57.355
Ma'am, no, you can't go out there.

14:57.438 --> 15:00.191
- That could be a poisonous gas cloud.
- Didn't you hear that man screaming?

15:00.274 --> 15:03.069
I agree. Let's stay here
until we figure it out.

15:03.152 --> 15:04.362
You're not listening!

15:05.196 --> 15:06.864
I can't stay here.

15:07.782 --> 15:11.661
Wanda's looking after little Victor.
She's only 8.

15:11.744 --> 15:15.999
Sometimes she forgets she's supposed to
be watching him, you know?

15:19.502 --> 15:22.380
I told them I'd only be gone
a few minutes.

15:23.381 --> 15:25.383
She's only 8!

15:26.551 --> 15:29.554
For their sakes, don't.

15:34.475 --> 15:36.602
Well, is anybody gonna help me?

15:39.647 --> 15:41.607
It's okay, pal.

15:42.692 --> 15:45.528
Won't somebody here see a lady home?

15:50.324 --> 15:51.367
You?

15:59.083 --> 16:00.293
You?

16:09.927 --> 16:11.137
It's okay, buddy.

16:11.220 --> 16:13.139
- You?
- Ma'am, please.

16:13.890 --> 16:15.725
I got my own boy to worry about.

16:19.562 --> 16:21.939
I hope you all rot in hell.

16:22.023 --> 16:24.067
- Ma'am, please, wait until--
- Get off of me.

16:59.185 --> 17:01.813
Okay, let's start cleaning up, okay?

17:01.896 --> 17:04.649
Get the spilled bottles,
broken glass, stuff like that.

17:04.732 --> 17:07.193
Aisle 3 has medical supplies.

17:07.276 --> 17:10.238
Okay, okay, it's okay.

17:10.321 --> 17:12.615
Easy champ, come on.

17:14.283 --> 17:15.701
All right, hey, hey, hey.

17:15.785 --> 17:17.829
You can't keep crying like this, pal.

17:17.912 --> 17:19.330
Come on.

17:19.413 --> 17:22.250
You're gonna hurt yourself.
Come on, you all right?

17:22.333 --> 17:23.376
I want Mommy.

17:23.459 --> 17:25.253
All right, I know you do. Okay.

17:27.463 --> 17:29.215
Just try to breathe, okay?

17:30.258 --> 17:32.426
Just try to breathe, pal, it's okay.

17:33.261 --> 17:34.262
It's all right.

17:36.305 --> 17:38.141
I haven't seen him
suck his thumb like this

17:38.224 --> 17:39.892
since he was two years old.

17:39.976 --> 17:41.686
He's in shock.

17:41.769 --> 17:43.354
I think we all are.

17:43.437 --> 17:45.022
You haven't met.

17:45.106 --> 17:46.440
Amanda Dunfrey.

17:46.524 --> 17:49.652
She's new in town as of this semester.

17:49.735 --> 17:51.445
Teaches 3rd grade,

17:51.529 --> 17:54.657
and the Special Ed kids
now that Mosher's retired.

17:54.740 --> 17:57.577
She's wonderful, the kids love her.

17:57.660 --> 18:00.121
And David's an artist,

18:00.204 --> 18:02.540
he does movie posters and such.

18:02.623 --> 18:03.916
And me.

18:04.625 --> 18:09.255
Lord, I'm babbling away
like some old biddy at a tea party.

18:09.338 --> 18:11.007
My nerves are jangled, I guess.

18:11.090 --> 18:12.258
Boy settle down?

18:12.341 --> 18:13.759
How is he?

18:13.843 --> 18:14.969
Still hot.

18:15.052 --> 18:16.888
Why don't I get him some aspirin?

18:16.971 --> 18:17.972
Aisle 3.

18:18.055 --> 18:19.557
- Okay.
- Thanks.

18:20.808 --> 18:22.059
How's Dan?

18:22.143 --> 18:23.644
His nose stopped bleeding.

18:23.728 --> 18:26.272
He's calmer now,
somebody gave him a Valium.

18:27.523 --> 18:29.901
I can't believe the way he ran in here.

18:29.984 --> 18:31.194
Never seen him like that.

18:31.277 --> 18:33.654
I need something to cover my boy up.

18:33.738 --> 18:35.323
You got any blankets?

18:35.406 --> 18:37.575
Furniture pads, loading dock.

18:37.658 --> 18:40.870
Gonna keep checking on people,
if you need anything, just holler.

18:40.953 --> 18:42.997
You bet. Sally, you mind?

18:43.080 --> 18:45.499
I'd love to.
I really should help him clean up.

18:45.583 --> 18:47.001
I'll take him.

18:47.084 --> 18:48.836
- Okay.
- Daddy, don't go!

18:48.920 --> 18:52.381
No, I'll be gone two seconds, Big Bill.
Come on, I'm gonna get your blanket.

18:52.465 --> 18:56.135
Mrs. Reppler's here,
and so is Mrs. Turman.

18:57.303 --> 18:58.930
I'll be close by, okay?

18:59.013 --> 19:01.307
Don't worry, I'm not far. Okay?

19:02.099 --> 19:03.434
Let me look at you.

19:08.564 --> 19:10.608
Wanna lie down?

19:10.691 --> 19:12.276
Yeah.

19:12.360 --> 19:13.527
There you go.

19:13.611 --> 19:17.156
As soon as it blows away,
we can walk out of here safe and free,

19:17.240 --> 19:18.741
but we have to be smarter.

19:18.824 --> 19:21.410
The first thing we need to do
is keep our wits about us

19:21.494 --> 19:22.954
and find out what's happening.

19:23.037 --> 19:24.872
Well, how we gonna do that, my man?

19:24.956 --> 19:27.333
We've got no phone signal.
We've got no radio.

19:27.416 --> 19:30.503
I'm sure they're working on
those problems as we speak.

19:30.586 --> 19:32.296
It stands to reason that
restoring communications

19:32.380 --> 19:33.381
would be their top priority.

20:08.374 --> 20:10.167
Oh, shit.

20:14.755 --> 20:16.007
Shit!

20:20.261 --> 20:22.013
Goddamn it!

20:25.224 --> 20:26.767
Bitch!

20:26.851 --> 20:30.021
It's obvious that we're in
some kind of natural disaster here.

20:30.104 --> 20:33.024
Ain't nothing obvious about
this son of a bitch from where I sit.

20:33.107 --> 20:35.192
There ain't nothing natural
about it either.

20:35.276 --> 20:36.360
That's right.

20:36.444 --> 20:39.196
It's Judgment Day,
and it's come round at last.

20:39.280 --> 20:41.449
There is nothing more obvious
or natural than that.

20:41.532 --> 20:43.326
Aw, fuck now.

20:43.409 --> 20:46.829
You've done that to yourself
by a life of sin and disillusion.

21:33.459 --> 21:35.336
- Hey, whoa!
- David!

21:35.419 --> 21:37.380
Hey, you guys hear that?

21:37.463 --> 21:39.632
The generator?
We're just gonna check it out.

21:39.715 --> 21:41.592
No, no, I turned the generator off,

21:42.218 --> 21:43.344
it was backing up.

21:44.762 --> 21:46.472
Nobody else heard that sound?

21:46.555 --> 21:47.640
What sound?

21:48.224 --> 21:52.103
I don't know, like a weird noise,

21:52.186 --> 21:53.896
back there in the dark.

21:53.979 --> 21:57.024
Like something was
pressing against the door.

21:57.108 --> 21:59.944
Did you hear it
before the lights went out or after?

22:00.027 --> 22:01.779
No, only after.

22:01.862 --> 22:04.073
After, but look, I heard it, okay?

22:04.156 --> 22:05.449
Nobody's calling you a liar.

22:05.533 --> 22:06.867
That's what it sounds like.

22:06.951 --> 22:09.245
No, no, no, no, now
don't be that way, Mr. Drayton.

22:09.328 --> 22:11.247
You had a scare, no doubt.

22:11.330 --> 22:13.165
Let's say we all go check it out.

22:13.249 --> 22:14.458
Here.

22:22.716 --> 22:23.801
Man.

22:23.884 --> 22:25.636
It's pretty rank in here.

22:25.719 --> 22:26.720
Myron, go check it out.

22:26.804 --> 22:27.805
All right.

22:30.516 --> 22:32.101
Go on, fire it up.

22:41.277 --> 22:44.280
All right, turn it off!

22:45.072 --> 22:47.074
Holy crow, don't that stink.

22:47.992 --> 22:51.120
Something's got the exhaust vent
plugged up from the outside.

22:51.203 --> 22:53.747
You get it running long enough
to raise that door a little,

22:53.831 --> 22:55.249
I'll go out and clear
whatever's blocking it.

22:55.332 --> 22:57.293
- No, no, you can't do that.
- Why not?

22:57.376 --> 22:58.502
It's an electric door, right?

22:58.586 --> 23:01.464
Well, yeah, but it may not be wise
to send him out there.

23:01.547 --> 23:02.882
Okay, I'll do it.

23:02.965 --> 23:05.426
No, look, it's not about
who goes out there--

23:05.509 --> 23:07.052
What, don't you think I can do it?

23:07.136 --> 23:09.680
Hey, I want to go, it was my idea.

23:09.763 --> 23:11.849
Whoa, wait, wait, just stop, okay?

23:11.932 --> 23:12.975
Jim, right?

23:13.058 --> 23:14.268
Myron?

23:14.351 --> 23:15.895
You guys are...

23:15.978 --> 23:17.771
Well, you don't seem to understand,

23:17.855 --> 23:19.482
or you're trying real hard not to.

23:19.565 --> 23:21.942
This isn't an ordinary mist, okay?

23:22.026 --> 23:24.612
You open that door and
something gets in here--

23:24.695 --> 23:26.530
Like what?

23:26.614 --> 23:28.741
Well, like whatever made
that noise I heard.

23:28.824 --> 23:30.618
Are you guys being willfully dense?

23:30.701 --> 23:32.745
Mr. Drayton, you know, pardon me,

23:32.828 --> 23:36.373
but I'm not convinced
that you heard anything.

23:36.457 --> 23:38.292
I mean, we're not hearing
anything now, right?

23:38.375 --> 23:39.460
Anybody?

23:40.544 --> 23:41.879
See?

23:43.088 --> 23:45.925
Now, I know, I know,
you're a big shot artist

23:46.008 --> 23:48.636
with connections in New York
and Hollywood and all that,

23:48.719 --> 23:50.471
but that don't make you
better than anybody else,

23:50.554 --> 23:52.389
- not in my book.
- Hey, I didn't say that.

23:52.473 --> 23:54.975
Nor do I like being talked down to
or called stupid

23:55.059 --> 23:57.895
by a guy who went to college
just 'cause he's got the jitters.

23:57.978 --> 24:00.397
Fellas, it doesn't even
matter about the generator,

24:00.481 --> 24:02.066
the food will keep without it.

24:02.149 --> 24:04.485
Kid, I'm gonna start the motor,
you raise the door,

24:04.568 --> 24:06.070
and you yell out when you got enough room.

24:06.153 --> 24:07.696
Yeah. Okay, good.

24:07.780 --> 24:08.822
Wait!

24:10.950 --> 24:12.785
You guys are gonna
let this kid risk his life

24:12.868 --> 24:14.370
over a generator that doesn't even matter?

24:14.453 --> 24:16.914
- Would you just shut the fuck up already?
- Norm!

24:16.997 --> 24:19.124
Listen, Mr. Drayton, I tell you what.

24:19.208 --> 24:22.503
The next time you got something to say,
you count your teeth.

24:22.586 --> 24:25.965
Because I'm sick to death
of your bullshit.

24:26.048 --> 24:27.508
All right?

24:27.591 --> 24:29.218
- Come on, Myron.
- This is crazy!

24:29.301 --> 24:30.553
Leave 'em be.

24:30.636 --> 24:33.055
What am I,
impugning their manhood or something?

24:33.138 --> 24:35.182
Listen, they've lost
their sense of proportion.

24:35.266 --> 24:36.308
What's going on here?

24:36.392 --> 24:38.185
Out there in the market
they were scared and confused.

24:38.269 --> 24:42.273
In here, there's a problem they can solve.
So, they're goddamn gonna solve it.

24:42.356 --> 24:43.857
- Ready, kid?
- Let's rock!

24:43.941 --> 24:45.276
Norm, come on.

24:45.359 --> 24:46.402
Don't, man.

24:50.447 --> 24:51.699
It's a mistake.

24:56.495 --> 24:57.496
Pussy.

25:02.167 --> 25:03.168
Hold up!

25:25.649 --> 25:28.068
So, any boogeyman?

25:31.071 --> 25:33.365
Pretty scary, ain't it, Norm?

25:33.449 --> 25:34.700
Yeah, right.

25:37.953 --> 25:39.079
Norm.

25:40.164 --> 25:41.290
Norm!

25:42.249 --> 25:43.626
What the fuck?

25:43.709 --> 25:44.710
Get it off, get it off!

25:44.793 --> 25:46.670
Get this friggin' thing off me!

25:46.754 --> 25:47.963
Get it off!

25:48.047 --> 25:49.715
Help me, help me, help me!

26:04.063 --> 26:06.607
There's more. There's more!

26:07.399 --> 26:08.609
Somebody help me.

26:10.361 --> 26:12.321
Somebody help me.

26:12.404 --> 26:14.865
What the fuck are you waiting for?

26:26.377 --> 26:27.378
Hang on!

26:37.930 --> 26:40.557
Hold him still!

26:48.565 --> 26:51.318
Jesus...

27:23.976 --> 27:25.310
Shit, shit!

27:26.186 --> 27:27.312
Shit!

27:29.565 --> 27:31.066
Dave, it's no good!

27:33.444 --> 27:35.696
Start the generator!

28:04.808 --> 28:05.851
Shit!

28:43.639 --> 28:45.057
Hey, I'm sorry.

28:47.893 --> 28:51.188
But how the hell was I supposed
to know what you meant?

28:52.856 --> 28:54.733
You said you heard something.

28:55.484 --> 28:58.821
How was I supposed to know what you meant?
You should've said what you meant better.

28:58.904 --> 29:01.907
I don't know, I thought maybe
it was a big bird or something.

29:02.699 --> 29:04.326
You got that kid killed.

29:04.910 --> 29:06.703
Did you get a good look at it, huh?

29:06.787 --> 29:09.790
Did you get a good look at what you did?

29:09.873 --> 29:10.874
Huh?

29:10.958 --> 29:12.292
David! Don't hit him anymore!

29:12.376 --> 29:14.086
- And you too! Assholes!
- It doesn't solve anything.

29:14.169 --> 29:17.881
You got that kid killed,
and I got his fucking blood on me!

29:36.984 --> 29:38.944
Okay, I'm done.

29:40.988 --> 29:41.989
Okay.

29:45.659 --> 29:46.910
What's next?

29:47.536 --> 29:48.996
Kill the generator.

29:49.872 --> 29:51.290
That's the first thing.

29:54.918 --> 29:56.295
I'm sorry.

30:00.966 --> 30:02.759
Jesus Christ. Oh, God.

30:04.177 --> 30:06.346
I'm sorry about the kid.

30:07.514 --> 30:09.850
Oh, God. Oh, God. Oh, God.

30:11.435 --> 30:13.604
We oughta get outta here.

30:16.899 --> 30:18.400
Hey, man, we didn't twist this on him.

30:18.483 --> 30:20.652
Yeah, he's a fuckin' kid.

30:20.736 --> 30:22.696
He's supposed to be stupid.

30:22.779 --> 30:24.781
What's your excuse, huh?

30:27.951 --> 30:29.202
Get outta here.

30:30.329 --> 30:32.706
Go back in the market, stay by the door.

30:34.416 --> 30:36.418
Don't say anything to anybody.

30:38.128 --> 30:39.129
Not yet.

30:40.797 --> 30:41.965
Not yet.

30:56.647 --> 30:58.231
Shit.

30:58.315 --> 30:59.524
David?

30:59.608 --> 31:01.151
Need a little light here.

31:11.954 --> 31:13.580
We have to tell 'em.

31:13.664 --> 31:14.790
The people in the market,

31:14.873 --> 31:17.626
we have to stop them from going outside.

31:17.709 --> 31:19.294
They won't believe us.

31:20.212 --> 31:21.421
They have to.

31:21.505 --> 31:24.132
I'm not sure I believe it. I was here.

31:24.967 --> 31:27.177
What we saw was impossible.

31:27.260 --> 31:28.887
You know that, don't you?

31:28.971 --> 31:32.557
I mean, what do we say?

31:33.934 --> 31:36.770
How do we convince them?

31:39.606 --> 31:43.819
Ollie, what the hell were those tentacles
even attached to?

31:49.366 --> 31:51.660
Oh, my God. Are you all right?

31:51.743 --> 31:54.329
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
it's not my blood, I'm fine.

31:54.413 --> 31:55.497
What the hell happened?

31:55.580 --> 31:57.874
I'll explain. Give me a minute, okay?

31:57.958 --> 32:00.127
I need to deal with something first.

32:01.545 --> 32:03.213
Please, I've got to...

32:03.296 --> 32:06.466
I can't let Billy see me like this,
he's scared enough.

32:06.550 --> 32:08.468
Just give me a minute,
keep him distracted.

32:08.552 --> 32:10.262
- Okay?
- Okay.

32:15.809 --> 32:17.227
Hey, look.

32:17.310 --> 32:18.812
I'm sorry about Norm.

32:18.895 --> 32:20.147
Me too.

32:20.230 --> 32:22.816
I mean, I ain't making excuses,
I'm just saying.

32:22.899 --> 32:24.234
Look, we need to tell people.

32:24.317 --> 32:26.653
We don't need to say how it went down
or anything like that,

32:26.737 --> 32:29.406
but we're in the deep shit here.

32:29.489 --> 32:30.907
People need to know.

32:30.991 --> 32:32.367
What about the out-of-towners?

32:32.451 --> 32:33.994
We've got plenty of them in the store.

32:34.077 --> 32:36.288
- Where do we even start?
- Brent Norton?

32:36.371 --> 32:38.165
That windbag?

32:38.248 --> 32:40.542
He's an important attorney in New York.

32:40.625 --> 32:42.627
That fella could be on the bench one day.

32:42.711 --> 32:45.297
Counts a lot for people
in this town, or anywhere.

32:45.380 --> 32:46.882
- Yeah, that's right.
- Do it quick, David.

32:46.965 --> 32:50.135
We've gotta discuss how we're gonna
stop that thing getting in here.

32:50.218 --> 32:52.304
Wait, what do you mean getting in?

32:52.387 --> 32:54.014
You shut the loading door.

32:54.097 --> 32:57.350
Yeah, but the entire front
of the store is plate glass.

33:01.605 --> 33:02.856
Jesus Christ.

33:15.869 --> 33:17.287
Listen.

33:17.370 --> 33:20.082
That guy who came in here
with the bloody nose.

33:25.629 --> 33:27.422
They're, they're...

33:27.506 --> 33:29.091
We saw tentacles.

33:29.174 --> 33:30.926
It ain't going very well, is it?

33:33.970 --> 33:35.806
- You what?
- Come here.

33:36.890 --> 33:38.141
Come here.

33:40.393 --> 33:41.436
Tell him.

33:43.313 --> 33:44.523
It's true.

33:51.446 --> 33:53.573
Tentacles. Yeah.

34:02.791 --> 34:05.919
Gentlemen, I'm sorry,

34:06.002 --> 34:08.046
I'm just not that stupid.

34:08.130 --> 34:11.258
I mean, what do you take me for?
I'm shocked.

34:12.050 --> 34:13.927
I'm shocked. I'm shocked.

34:14.010 --> 34:16.138
It's pretty tasteless
using what's happening here

34:16.221 --> 34:17.639
to try to make me look like an idiot.

34:17.722 --> 34:19.307
No, no, no,
that's not what's going on here.

34:19.391 --> 34:22.435
Look, come back to the loading dock,
okay? I'll show you.

34:22.519 --> 34:26.189
Blood, and a chuck of tentacle
on the floor.

34:26.273 --> 34:28.358
- No.
- No? What do you mean no?

34:28.441 --> 34:31.444
No. We've got real problems
to deal with here,

34:31.528 --> 34:35.907
and this pathetic attempt at a joke
has gone far enough.

34:35.991 --> 34:37.701
Mr. Norton.

34:37.784 --> 34:41.163
- What reason could we possibly have--
- Please, please!

34:41.246 --> 34:43.832
This is payback for the lawsuit
that I filed against him last year,

34:43.915 --> 34:45.792
and you guys are backing him up.

34:45.876 --> 34:47.210
So, winning wasn't enough, huh?

34:47.294 --> 34:49.713
You wanted to humiliate me some more.

34:49.796 --> 34:53.300
Show me a rubber snake while these hicks
stand around laughing their asses off.

34:53.383 --> 34:55.302
- Watch who you're calling a hick.
- Myron, Myron!

34:55.385 --> 34:57.220
- Hey, hey, fuck--
- Mr. Norton, I swear.

34:57.304 --> 34:59.389
You've got us all wrong.

34:59.472 --> 35:03.977
You're not too crazy
about out-of-towners, are ya?

35:04.853 --> 35:06.938
I only spend my money
and I pay my taxes here,

35:07.022 --> 35:11.318
and I've seen you talking behind my back.

35:12.569 --> 35:14.779
How y'all stick together?

35:17.199 --> 35:18.909
Well, don't I feel foolish?

35:18.992 --> 35:21.411
I actually thought you were
being kind to me today.

35:21.494 --> 35:22.996
Well, thanks for setting me straight.

35:23.079 --> 35:25.332
And I'm glad that tree fell
on your boathouse, you know that?

35:25.415 --> 35:28.043
Glad. Smashed it in pretty good,
didn't it? Fantastic.

35:28.126 --> 35:29.794
Now all of y'all, just stay out of my way-

35:29.878 --> 35:32.214
I know you're scared, man. I'm scared too.

35:32.297 --> 35:33.715
Lives are at stake around here.

35:33.798 --> 35:35.091
- David, I--
- Okay, my son's life.

35:35.175 --> 35:36.426
Now, I need you.

35:36.509 --> 35:38.678
Brent, please,

35:38.762 --> 35:40.847
get your head out of your ass. All right?

35:40.931 --> 35:43.433
I'll drag you back there if I have to.
Come here.

35:43.516 --> 35:44.726
- David, get your--
- No, I need--

35:44.809 --> 35:46.561
Get your goddamn hands off of me!

35:46.645 --> 35:49.105
I'll sue your ass again! Sue your ass!

35:49.189 --> 35:50.774
And this time you'll go to jail.

35:50.857 --> 35:52.359
This man assaulted me.

35:52.442 --> 35:54.903
He assaulted me. You were witness to it.

35:54.986 --> 35:57.030
- This man's crazy, he's crazy.
- No.

35:57.781 --> 36:00.283
He isn't. I wish he was, but he isn't.

36:02.494 --> 36:04.621
Everyone in the store.

36:04.704 --> 36:06.623
You want to come back here?

36:07.457 --> 36:10.335
There's something that you need to hear.
It concerns you all.

36:11.211 --> 36:12.712
- Okay?
- Wait, wait, wait, wait.

36:12.796 --> 36:14.965
I don't know what you people
think you're doing.

36:15.674 --> 36:18.134
You drinking? For Chrissake, Ollie.

36:19.177 --> 36:21.972
Do you want me to report you?
You want to lose your job?

36:22.055 --> 36:23.974
Look, I'm gonna be taking down names,
starting with you.

36:24.057 --> 36:26.017
And I am prepared to file a police report.

36:26.101 --> 36:28.937
- Fine, Bud, write down your names.
- I will.

36:29.020 --> 36:32.732
And in the meantime,
shut the fuck up and listen.

36:32.816 --> 36:34.442
This is Mr. David Drayton.

36:34.526 --> 36:37.404
You need to hear what he's got to say
if you're thinking about leaving.

36:37.487 --> 36:41.074
Go hang out with the ladies, all right?
Listen, don't be scared.

36:42.742 --> 36:43.743
It's okay.

36:45.912 --> 36:47.038
Okay.

36:48.081 --> 36:49.624
This is how it is.

36:49.708 --> 36:52.794
Now, I don't know what this mist is,

36:52.877 --> 36:55.338
but there are things in it
and they're dangerous, like Dan said.

36:55.422 --> 36:57.090
That's right.

36:57.173 --> 36:58.633
That's exactly right.

36:58.717 --> 37:00.593
What kinda things?

37:00.677 --> 37:02.595
I never saw it. It happened too fast.

37:02.679 --> 37:04.514
I got knocked down.

37:04.597 --> 37:06.766
Five us went back in the loading dock.

37:07.517 --> 37:11.354
It was Jim, Myron, Ollie, me,

37:12.105 --> 37:13.732
Norm, the bag boy.

37:13.815 --> 37:15.900
- And we opened the door--
- Where's Norm?

37:15.984 --> 37:20.447
So Norm could go out
and clear the vent for the generator.

37:20.530 --> 37:22.324
Something came out of the mist
and took him.

37:22.407 --> 37:24.784
Took him? What do you mean?

37:26.369 --> 37:27.495
Just killed him.

37:27.579 --> 37:29.456
I mean, dragged him off.

37:29.539 --> 37:34.085
Now, guys, I don't know
what these things are.

37:35.086 --> 37:36.963
All we saw were tentacles.

37:40.467 --> 37:41.634
Tentacles?

37:44.971 --> 37:46.348
Tentacles, he says.

37:47.057 --> 37:49.100
Tentacles from planet X.

37:49.184 --> 37:50.393
No, it's a lie, you know.

37:50.477 --> 37:53.646
All these people do
is just lie each other up.

37:53.730 --> 37:54.731
It's a pile of shit.

37:54.814 --> 37:57.400
Of course it's a lie.
Of course it's a lie, it's lunacy!

37:58.318 --> 38:01.363
And from the look of it, the tentacles
are coming out of the beer cans.

38:01.446 --> 38:04.282
All right, Bud,
don't take our word for it. Go look.

38:17.295 --> 38:19.297
What the hell is that?

38:50.870 --> 38:56.042
It appears we may have a problem
of some magnitude here.

39:23.945 --> 39:25.113
Let me...

39:27.115 --> 39:30.452
help these people.

39:32.287 --> 39:34.539
Let me preach your word.

39:36.416 --> 39:38.918
Let me shine your light.

39:39.461 --> 39:42.464
'Cause they're not all bad.

39:42.547 --> 39:44.716
They can't all be bad.

39:47.969 --> 39:51.473
Some can be saved, can't they?

39:52.140 --> 39:55.435
Yes, some can be brought

39:56.394 --> 39:59.522
to heaven's holy gates through your grace.

39:59.606 --> 40:00.773
I have to believe that,

40:00.857 --> 40:05.403
though I know most people swim
in a lake of fire forever.

40:08.907 --> 40:10.825
If I can save a few,

40:12.118 --> 40:13.995
even one,

40:15.163 --> 40:17.790
then my life will have counted
for something.

40:18.416 --> 40:21.461
I will have pulled my weight,

40:21.544 --> 40:24.714
I will have earned my place at your side,

40:24.797 --> 40:29.511
I will have served a purpose
here on this earth.

40:29.594 --> 40:31.012
Hello?

40:46.986 --> 40:48.071
What?

40:48.154 --> 40:50.365
I just need to use the bathroom.

40:52.784 --> 40:55.036
Okay, well then, have at it.

40:59.123 --> 41:00.583
Ma'am,

41:01.751 --> 41:04.629
I just want you to know that it's okay.

41:05.463 --> 41:07.340
Being scared, I mean.

41:07.423 --> 41:11.302
And, well, if you need a friend, you know,

41:11.386 --> 41:12.929
someone to talk to-

41:13.012 --> 41:16.641
I have a friend. God up above.

41:16.724 --> 41:18.393
I talk to him every day.

41:18.476 --> 41:20.645
Don't you condescend me.

41:20.728 --> 41:22.230
- I'm sorry?
- Not ever.

41:22.313 --> 41:25.316
You don't mock me.

41:25.400 --> 41:27.527
That's not what I was doing.

41:28.027 --> 41:30.154
Look, I tell you what.

41:30.238 --> 41:32.323
The day I need a friend like you,

41:32.407 --> 41:35.243
I'll just have myself a little squat
and shit one out.

41:40.915 --> 41:42.834
Maybe you do believe this.

41:42.917 --> 41:46.170
Maybe they're not lies.
They're delusions, whatever.

41:46.254 --> 41:50.133
The fact remains the evidence here
is flimsy. It's bordering on ludicrous.

41:50.216 --> 41:51.926
Hey, this isn't a courtroom.

41:52.010 --> 41:53.177
You're not arguing a case,

41:53.261 --> 41:55.221
and you're doing nothing but damage,
talking the way you are.

41:55.305 --> 41:57.765
And you can throw as much cow's blood
around the loading dock as you want to.

41:57.849 --> 41:59.475
You still haven't fooled anyone.

41:59.559 --> 42:01.519
Leave it alone, David.
You can't convince some people

42:01.603 --> 42:04.147
there's a fire
even when their hair is burning.

42:04.230 --> 42:05.940
Denial is a powerful thing.

42:06.024 --> 42:07.066
Well, keep talking.

42:07.150 --> 42:10.820
I'll have no part of it,
nor would any thinking person.

42:10.903 --> 42:12.864
Keep thinking, Mr. Lawyer.

42:13.698 --> 42:16.117
There's no defense
against the will of God.

42:16.200 --> 42:18.411
There's no court of appeals in hell.

42:18.494 --> 42:20.788
There's no defense here either,

42:20.872 --> 42:23.666
not even with all the fertilizer
in the world.

42:23.750 --> 42:25.668
Not even if you stack it
as high as you can,

42:25.752 --> 42:28.838
it's still just bags of shit, isn't it?

42:28.921 --> 42:30.757
Those of you who want to
discuss this thing rationally

42:30.840 --> 42:34.302
to find a means of rescue
are welcome to join me.

42:34.385 --> 42:38.931
Those who want to stack dog food,
knock yourselves out.

42:42.769 --> 42:44.937
We got those windows taped up
as best we could,

42:45.021 --> 42:46.230
it should help.

42:46.314 --> 42:48.107
Yeah, I think so.

42:49.525 --> 42:52.028
Duct tape and dog food bags.

42:53.196 --> 42:54.989
That bad?

42:55.073 --> 42:56.157
It's not good.

42:56.240 --> 43:00.495
There's none so blind
as those who will not see.

43:00.578 --> 43:02.163
Open your eyes.

43:02.246 --> 43:04.540
Let the scales fall away.

43:04.624 --> 43:06.793
This has all been written.

43:08.252 --> 43:11.422
Revelations, chapter 15.

43:11.506 --> 43:14.050
"And the temple was filled with smoke

43:14.133 --> 43:17.553
from the glory of God, and from his power.

43:17.637 --> 43:19.430
And no one could enter the temple

43:19.514 --> 43:23.768
until the seven plagues
of the seven angels were completed."

43:23.851 --> 43:25.520
Well, what are you saying?

43:25.603 --> 43:26.938
What are you proposing?

43:27.021 --> 43:31.818
That we all prepare to meet our maker.

43:31.901 --> 43:34.570
Prepare to meet shit.

43:34.654 --> 43:37.198
Lady, your tongue must
be hung in the middle

43:37.281 --> 43:39.200
so that it could waggle at both ends.

43:39.283 --> 43:41.285
No, the end time has come.

43:41.369 --> 43:43.454
Not in flames, but in mist.

43:43.538 --> 43:45.206
- Come here!
- Easy, man!

43:45.289 --> 43:49.877
How about if your ass prepares to meet
my size 10 work boot, how about that?

43:49.961 --> 43:51.170
Hey, there's no call for that.

43:51.254 --> 43:53.589
Yeah, Myron, please,
calm your friend down.

43:53.673 --> 43:56.426
I'm trying to save your soul,
you stupid man.

43:56.509 --> 43:58.720
- Doubters will doubt till the end.
- Don't worry, Billy, it's okay.

43:58.803 --> 44:02.515
A monstrosity did pull that poor boy away.

44:03.224 --> 44:04.726
Things in the mist.

44:04.809 --> 44:06.436
Do you doubt?

44:06.519 --> 44:07.645
Do you?

44:09.063 --> 44:10.064
Then go out.

44:11.149 --> 44:13.443
Go out and say, "How do you do?"

44:13.526 --> 44:14.819
Shut up, lady!

44:16.404 --> 44:17.572
For God's sakes!

44:17.655 --> 44:19.657
Look, you'll have to stop now.
You're scaring the children.

44:19.741 --> 44:21.159
They should be scared.

44:21.242 --> 44:23.411
Yes, they should.

44:25.037 --> 44:27.623
Their beautiful, pure little minds

44:27.707 --> 44:30.877
have been corrupted with lies, lies.

44:30.960 --> 44:34.380
All this talk of a modern God, or no God.

44:36.215 --> 44:37.759
There is one God:

44:37.842 --> 44:39.802
The God of the Israelites.

44:39.886 --> 44:42.430
And he is a stern and vengeful God.

44:42.513 --> 44:45.057
And we have been mocking him far too long.

44:45.141 --> 44:48.853
And now he demands retribution and blood.

44:48.936 --> 44:52.064
It is time to declare yourselves.

44:52.148 --> 44:55.234
Take sides, the saved and the damned.

44:55.318 --> 44:58.613
Read the Good Book.
It calls for expiation.

44:58.696 --> 44:59.697
Blood!

44:59.781 --> 45:01.657
- What?
- Blood.

45:02.950 --> 45:04.660
Little Normie was first,

45:04.744 --> 45:07.914
and now God calls the rest of us.

45:07.997 --> 45:09.499
The bill is due.

45:09.582 --> 45:10.917
It must be paid.

45:11.000 --> 45:14.045
As Abraham prepared
to sacrifice his only son

45:14.128 --> 45:15.963
to prove his love for God, so...

45:16.047 --> 45:17.048
Enough.

45:23.346 --> 45:25.389
Another down payment.

45:25.473 --> 45:26.891
A few more pennies in the jar.

45:26.974 --> 45:27.975
Now that's nice.

45:28.059 --> 45:29.977
See, I can't smack her,
but it's okay for you?

45:30.061 --> 45:32.438
I'm sorry, everybody,
but this lady's perspective

45:32.522 --> 45:34.774
is a little too Old Testament
for my tastes.

45:34.857 --> 45:36.108
They'll come for you.

45:37.360 --> 45:39.362
Maybe tonight when darkness comes.

45:41.113 --> 45:42.532
They'll come tonight.

45:43.115 --> 45:44.784
And they'll take someone else.

45:44.867 --> 45:46.536
See if they don't.

45:46.619 --> 45:50.998
And when they do, you will cry to God,

45:51.082 --> 45:54.669
and you will beg Mother Carmody
to show you the way.

45:54.752 --> 45:55.795
That's fine.

45:56.921 --> 45:59.048
Until then, if you don't shut up,

45:59.131 --> 46:01.300
I'll wrap this tape around your mouth.

46:01.384 --> 46:03.636
You just try it, Ollie Weeks.

46:03.719 --> 46:04.971
And you, bitch.

46:06.681 --> 46:10.226
You hit me again, if you dare.

46:11.435 --> 46:14.480
You'll be on your knees to me
before this is through.

46:20.903 --> 46:22.655
Those of you who aren't locals should know

46:22.738 --> 46:27.535
that Mrs. Carmody is known in town
for being unstable.

46:27.618 --> 46:28.661
No shit.

46:29.495 --> 46:31.122
What was your first clue?

46:36.460 --> 46:38.337
Hi.

46:38.421 --> 46:39.630
Sup, little dude?

46:39.714 --> 46:41.424
How come your friends don't come get us?

46:41.507 --> 46:44.427
They got tanks and stuff, right?

46:44.510 --> 46:45.845
Why can't you just call 'em?

46:45.928 --> 46:47.305
Phones don't work.

46:47.388 --> 46:48.890
But don't you got, like, a radio?

46:48.973 --> 46:50.766
Hey, champ. What's going on?

46:50.850 --> 46:52.685
I want their friends to come rescue us.

46:52.768 --> 46:55.021
They would if they could, pal,
they're stuck here just like us.

46:55.104 --> 46:56.314
But--

46:56.397 --> 46:58.190
Guys, we could use a hand over there.

46:58.274 --> 47:00.943
Yeah, sure thing. Troop, off your asses.

47:01.027 --> 47:03.821
- You all right?
- I don't like that scary lady.

47:03.905 --> 47:06.282
Man, I don't either.

47:06.365 --> 47:08.284
But you know what?

47:08.367 --> 47:10.286
Maybe she's scared too.

47:11.203 --> 47:12.330
You think?

47:13.456 --> 47:15.541
You think Mommy's okay?

47:17.126 --> 47:18.169
Billy...

47:20.963 --> 47:23.215
I'm sorry about the times
I was bad to her.

47:23.299 --> 47:24.425
Hey.

47:25.343 --> 47:27.511
Mommy loves you very much,

47:28.429 --> 47:30.181
and I bet she's fine.

47:32.099 --> 47:35.519
And I promise you,
I'm gonna do everything I can

47:35.603 --> 47:37.438
to get us back to her.

47:38.481 --> 47:39.982
- Okay?
- Okay.

47:40.816 --> 47:41.817
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

47:43.486 --> 47:46.280
So we can use the charcoal fluid

47:46.364 --> 47:47.531
and the mops to make torches,

47:47.615 --> 47:49.617
and we've got knives and stuff, God knows.

47:49.700 --> 47:51.494
This may be a silly question, Bud,

47:51.577 --> 47:55.915
but do you happen
to have a gun in the store?

47:55.998 --> 47:57.625
- Here?
- No.

47:57.708 --> 47:59.585
Please, this isn't Los Angeles.

47:59.669 --> 48:02.588
I've got a shotgun in my truck.

48:02.672 --> 48:04.131
I could try for it if you want.

48:04.215 --> 48:06.467
God, I don't think that would be
a good idea, Mr. Cornell.

48:06.550 --> 48:07.718
Hold on.

48:10.012 --> 48:13.307
This gun. My husband's idea.

48:14.058 --> 48:16.811
He's away on business a lot.
It's not even loaded.

48:16.894 --> 48:19.063
Ain't much use unloaded, ma'am.

48:23.150 --> 48:24.485
You know how to use that?

48:24.568 --> 48:26.570
Well, I shot it once on a pistol range,

48:26.654 --> 48:28.572
hit the target a few times.

48:28.656 --> 48:30.491
So, we've got a gun.

48:31.701 --> 48:33.703
Anybody know how to shoot it?

48:33.786 --> 48:35.121
Well, I mean?

48:35.204 --> 48:36.330
I do.

48:38.791 --> 48:39.792
You?

48:40.960 --> 48:42.128
Ollie, please.

48:48.050 --> 48:49.927
Some target shooting.

48:50.011 --> 48:52.179
State champion in '94.

48:52.263 --> 48:55.933
- Hey, you're crazy if you go out there.
- Let us pass! Let us pass, please!

48:56.017 --> 48:57.184
Let's just talk this thing through.

48:57.268 --> 48:59.645
We have, and we made
our decision. We're leaving.

48:59.729 --> 49:02.523
Hey, Mr. Mackey's gonna barbecue
some chicken on the gas grill.

49:02.606 --> 49:03.649
Why don't we just sit down and--

49:03.733 --> 49:05.026
What, and let you keep on talking?

49:05.109 --> 49:07.111
No, I've been in far too many court rooms
to fall for that.

49:07.194 --> 49:09.280
You've already psyched out half a dozen
of my people already.

49:09.363 --> 49:12.450
Your people? What kind of talk is that?
They are people, that's all.

49:12.533 --> 49:13.784
Now, listen, everyone.

49:13.868 --> 49:17.038
We are experiencing some kind of disaster.

49:17.121 --> 49:19.123
I don't know whether
it's man-made or natural,

49:19.206 --> 49:23.961
but I do know that it's definitely
not supernatural, or Biblical.

49:24.045 --> 49:25.254
And no offense, Mrs. Carmody,

49:25.337 --> 49:29.175
but the only way we're gonna
help ourselves is to seek rescue.

49:30.885 --> 49:32.136
We're going out.

49:34.221 --> 49:35.222
Brent, look.

49:35.306 --> 49:37.266
- I'm not discussing this any further.
- I know.

49:37.349 --> 49:39.018
I just want to ask a favor.

49:40.144 --> 49:41.771
Tie this around your waist.

49:41.854 --> 49:43.230
What for?

49:43.314 --> 49:45.483
It'll let us know you got
at least 300 feet.

49:47.401 --> 49:48.402
I'll do it.

49:49.945 --> 49:51.906
Are you throwing in with them?

49:51.989 --> 49:53.699
Me? No thanks.

49:53.783 --> 49:56.368
I think your man there's
a little too tightly wound.

49:56.452 --> 49:58.412
Gonna get somebody killed.

49:58.496 --> 50:01.832
I'm thinking we could use
that shotgun of yours.

50:01.916 --> 50:04.043
I saw where you parked when I pulled in.

50:04.126 --> 50:05.252
Red pickup, right?

50:05.336 --> 50:06.754
Far entrance?

50:06.837 --> 50:08.547
Son, you've got brass balls.

50:09.423 --> 50:14.553
The shells are in the glove compartment.
Drive it back.

50:14.637 --> 50:15.805
All right.

50:15.888 --> 50:17.556
Just see they're paying out this line.

50:17.640 --> 50:19.892
Line's up, I'll cut her loose.

50:19.975 --> 50:21.352
Just so you understand.

50:21.435 --> 50:22.686
Yeah.

50:30.111 --> 50:32.446
You sure there's no way
I can talk you out of this?

50:32.530 --> 50:36.283
David, there's nothing out there.

50:36.367 --> 50:37.827
Nothing in the mist.

50:37.910 --> 50:40.538
What if you were wrong?

50:40.621 --> 50:46.669
Then I guess the joke
would be on me after all.

50:52.800 --> 50:55.094
We're gonna send back help.

50:55.177 --> 50:58.097
You'll die out there, all of you.

51:10.234 --> 51:11.610
Hey, crazy lady.

51:11.694 --> 51:13.445
I believe in God too.

51:13.529 --> 51:16.073
I just don't think he's
the bloodthirsty asshole

51:16.157 --> 51:17.491
you make him out to be.

51:17.575 --> 51:20.327
Well, you take that up with the devil
when you run into him.

51:20.411 --> 51:22.496
Just chat it over at your leisure.

51:30.462 --> 51:34.717
Well, let's strike out
toward the center of town.

51:51.734 --> 51:53.194
Keep it loose.

52:09.168 --> 52:10.628
Nice and easy.

52:10.711 --> 52:12.046
Keep goin'.

52:29.939 --> 52:30.940
Look.

52:34.068 --> 52:35.319
It's goin'.

52:36.946 --> 52:38.322
They're doing good.

52:56.048 --> 52:57.258
Put it down!

52:59.927 --> 53:01.053
Pull!

53:03.931 --> 53:06.392
I'm slipping!

53:06.475 --> 53:07.476
Pull!

53:07.559 --> 53:10.521
Back up, back up, back up!

53:22.408 --> 53:23.742
Get it off!

53:32.876 --> 53:34.169
Oh, my God.

53:42.052 --> 53:44.763
Oh, my God.

53:48.058 --> 53:49.351
Oh, my God.

54:03.282 --> 54:04.575
Cut the rope!

54:07.369 --> 54:08.871
Shut the door!

54:14.126 --> 54:15.502
Now do you see?

54:18.130 --> 54:19.715
Now do you believe?

54:29.183 --> 54:32.102
About a half hour of daylight left.

54:32.186 --> 54:33.979
Guys, how's it going
with these work lights?

54:34.063 --> 54:36.148
We're getting them rigged up, all right.

54:36.231 --> 54:37.941
Yeah, check it out.

54:38.025 --> 54:40.569
All right, all right, save it, save it.

54:40.652 --> 54:42.237
These batteries ain't topped up.

54:42.321 --> 54:44.698
If you turn the lights on,
it's gonna drain them quick.

54:44.782 --> 54:46.700
- How quick?
- Five minutes, maybe 10?

54:46.784 --> 54:48.744
- Yeah, if that.
- Okay.

54:48.827 --> 54:50.120
Emergencies only.

54:50.704 --> 54:53.290
If something gets in the store.

55:01.131 --> 55:02.633
Holy Jesus, you scared the shit outta me.

55:02.716 --> 55:05.719
Sally, I'm sorry, really.

55:05.803 --> 55:08.555
I thought I'd come in and say hi
and see how you were holding up.

55:08.639 --> 55:09.848
- Hi.
- Hi.

55:11.058 --> 55:12.726
Barely, how about you?

55:12.810 --> 55:14.186
I'm worried about my folks, I guess.

55:14.269 --> 55:16.605
You know, they live up on Shorham Road.

55:16.688 --> 55:19.108
That's less than 5 miles from here.

55:19.191 --> 55:20.818
How about yours?

55:20.901 --> 55:23.362
They're out-of-town right now.

55:23.445 --> 55:25.989
They're at my aunt's in Boston, so...

55:26.073 --> 55:27.241
That's lucky.

55:27.324 --> 55:28.992
That means they're okay.

55:29.076 --> 55:30.077
I hope so.

55:32.413 --> 55:33.664
So...

55:34.289 --> 55:36.041
How soon you shippin' out?

55:36.125 --> 55:37.918
A couple weeks.

55:39.461 --> 55:42.423
Scared about going over there?

55:42.506 --> 55:43.924
Yeah.

55:48.554 --> 55:49.555
Hey, Wayne?

55:51.140 --> 55:53.308
How come you never asked me out?

55:53.976 --> 55:56.645
We flirted all through high school.
I know you like me.

56:00.816 --> 56:02.109
So, how come?

56:04.570 --> 56:06.405
I'm stupid, I guess.

56:23.046 --> 56:25.048
Oh, shit, I'm sorry.

56:25.132 --> 56:27.134
Don't be, I just...

56:27.217 --> 56:29.678
I just didn't really want it
to happen like this, you know?

56:29.761 --> 56:31.805
Some shitty locker room at work.

56:33.056 --> 56:35.225
Can we just stay in here a while then?

56:36.018 --> 56:38.270
Okay, just you and me?

56:49.740 --> 56:52.242
The parking lot lamps turned on.

56:52.326 --> 56:53.410
They're on a timer.

56:53.494 --> 56:55.662
Must be a different one that's live.

56:55.746 --> 56:58.081
Maybe we could tie into them somehow.

56:58.165 --> 57:01.126
Get some electricity in here.

57:01.210 --> 57:03.337
That would mean walking out the door.

57:14.306 --> 57:15.474
God!

57:15.557 --> 57:17.226
Oh, my God.

57:17.309 --> 57:19.853
- Billy, Billy.
- David!

57:23.524 --> 57:24.525
Look!

57:47.422 --> 57:49.383
My God.

58:04.898 --> 58:06.066
Bugs?

58:07.693 --> 58:10.237
Not like any I've ever seen.

58:10.320 --> 58:12.656
"They came out of the smoke.

58:12.739 --> 58:14.992
Locusts upon the earth.

58:15.075 --> 58:17.369
And unto them was given power,

58:17.452 --> 58:21.832
even as the scorpions of the earth
have power."

58:21.915 --> 58:23.709
Wow.

58:24.376 --> 58:26.295
Look at those stingers.

58:29.881 --> 58:31.842
Dear God.

59:10.922 --> 59:12.507
Holy shit!

59:28.565 --> 59:31.401
Myron, get the ones in the back.

59:31.485 --> 59:34.071
God, I think they're attracted
to the light.

59:34.154 --> 59:35.614
Look out, look out, look out!

59:35.697 --> 59:37.282
Douse the light!

59:38.450 --> 59:39.785
Look out, look out!

59:44.581 --> 59:45.832
Move, move!

59:47.834 --> 59:49.836
Light, light, light, light, light!

59:51.505 --> 59:55.300
"And there come a voice from the temple,
saying to the seven angels,

59:55.384 --> 59:57.761
'Go your ways,

59:57.844 --> 01:00:01.848
and pour out the vials of the wrath of God
upon the earth.'"

01:00:10.607 --> 01:00:13.360
Ollie, the glass is gonna give!

01:00:21.034 --> 01:00:22.035
- Shit.
- Oh, my God.

01:00:22.119 --> 01:00:23.787
They turned on all the lights.

01:00:23.870 --> 01:00:27.207
- Jim, Myron!
- Fire! Light it! Light it!

01:00:27.290 --> 01:00:28.750
Come on, come on!

01:00:32.963 --> 01:00:33.964
Whoa!

01:00:41.513 --> 01:00:43.098
Sally, look out!

01:00:53.817 --> 01:00:56.236
Let me see, sweetheart, let me see.

01:00:56.319 --> 01:00:58.363
No, you're gonna be okay,
you're gonna be okay.

01:00:58.447 --> 01:00:59.448
Let me see, let me see.

01:00:59.531 --> 01:01:01.199
You're fine, you're gonna be okay.

01:01:01.283 --> 01:01:03.201
Gimme the lighter, for the fire!

01:01:08.248 --> 01:01:10.709
Breathe, stay with me, Sally.
Sweetheart, come on, come on.

01:01:10.792 --> 01:01:13.086
Goddamn childproofing sons of bitches.

01:01:14.045 --> 01:01:17.007
Shit! Shit!

01:01:19.301 --> 01:01:20.469
Shoot it! Shoot it!

01:01:20.552 --> 01:01:22.179
I can't! I'll smash the window!

01:01:23.305 --> 01:01:24.306
God!

01:01:28.310 --> 01:01:30.061
- Go, go!
- Shit!

01:01:31.730 --> 01:01:33.565
Get down!

01:01:40.363 --> 01:01:41.406
Shit!

01:01:51.124 --> 01:01:53.543
- Ollie, you want these lights on or off?
- Leave them on!

01:01:59.382 --> 01:02:00.509
Oh, God!

01:02:02.385 --> 01:02:03.386
Kill it!

01:02:06.431 --> 01:02:07.682
Kill it!

01:02:11.978 --> 01:02:13.063
Bring torches!

01:02:13.146 --> 01:02:14.981
- We need something to keep 'em out!
- Come on!

01:02:16.942 --> 01:02:18.068
Sally!

01:02:29.996 --> 01:02:32.207
Where are the goddamn extinguishers?

01:02:42.884 --> 01:02:44.970
Get it, get it, get it!

01:02:49.683 --> 01:02:51.059
Bring torches!

01:02:51.142 --> 01:02:52.644
We need torches at the window!

01:02:52.727 --> 01:02:54.271
Plug that hole!

01:03:01.862 --> 01:03:03.280
Dad!

01:03:08.410 --> 01:03:10.328
Down, down, lay down!

01:03:27.012 --> 01:03:28.263
My life.

01:03:29.180 --> 01:03:30.932
My life for you,

01:03:31.016 --> 01:03:32.517
your will be done.

01:03:45.530 --> 01:03:47.490
- No!
- Daddy!

01:03:48.408 --> 01:03:50.035
Daddy!

01:04:05.300 --> 01:04:06.843
No!

01:04:06.927 --> 01:04:08.219
Daddy!

01:04:08.303 --> 01:04:09.763
- Billy!
- Daddy!

01:04:23.109 --> 01:04:24.277
Billy!

01:04:24.861 --> 01:04:26.029
Dad!

01:04:28.281 --> 01:04:30.784
- Dad!
- Billy, please!

01:04:36.957 --> 01:04:38.041
Billy!

01:05:10.657 --> 01:05:11.741
Bring some tape!

01:05:17.247 --> 01:05:19.666
Hurry up with the blankets!

01:05:19.749 --> 01:05:21.835
It hurts so bad!

01:05:30.552 --> 01:05:31.886
It hurts so bad!

01:05:36.891 --> 01:05:38.059
Did we get 'em?

01:05:38.143 --> 01:05:40.520
Did we get 'em all?

01:05:40.603 --> 01:05:42.480
She was right.

01:05:42.564 --> 01:05:44.899
She said that it would happen like this.

01:05:44.983 --> 01:05:47.944
She said that they would come at night.

01:05:48.028 --> 01:05:50.530
She told us someone would die.

01:06:15.138 --> 01:06:16.473
Mommy.

01:06:18.600 --> 01:06:19.601
It's okay.

01:06:20.268 --> 01:06:23.021
It's okay, it's just a dream.

01:06:23.104 --> 01:06:25.315
It's just a bad dream.

01:06:25.398 --> 01:06:26.983
I want my mommy.

01:06:27.567 --> 01:06:28.777
I know.

01:06:29.360 --> 01:06:32.280
I know, of course you do.

01:06:32.363 --> 01:06:34.157
I want to go home.

01:06:34.240 --> 01:06:35.408
Just sleep.

01:06:36.743 --> 01:06:40.455
Everything will be better in the morning.

01:06:45.251 --> 01:06:47.170
I think he likes you.

01:06:49.047 --> 01:06:51.716
Well, I hate that I had to lie to him.

01:06:52.926 --> 01:06:54.385
You have kids?

01:06:54.469 --> 01:06:55.553
No.

01:06:55.637 --> 01:07:00.683
I always wanted to,
but things haven't been working out.

01:07:03.061 --> 01:07:07.273
Right now I'm thinking
maybe that's for the best.

01:07:07.357 --> 01:07:10.985
I saw creatures fly
into the store tonight.

01:07:11.069 --> 01:07:12.570
They shouldn't exist.

01:07:13.947 --> 01:07:17.951
I keep thinking I'm gonna
wake up in a rubber room.

01:07:18.034 --> 01:07:20.245
You're not alone in that.

01:07:20.328 --> 01:07:22.831
We're all right there with you.

01:07:22.914 --> 01:07:25.583
This isn't gonna end, is it?

01:07:27.710 --> 01:07:28.711
David.

01:07:29.879 --> 01:07:32.006
It's Joe. He's getting worse.

01:07:51.109 --> 01:07:52.152
Joe.

01:07:53.778 --> 01:07:56.489
How you holdin' up, partner?

01:07:56.573 --> 01:07:58.825
David, is that you?

01:08:00.160 --> 01:08:02.787
Yeah, pal, how are doin'?

01:08:02.871 --> 01:08:04.622
It's bad, he's bad.

01:08:05.456 --> 01:08:08.501
I didn't know anything
could hurt like this.

01:08:08.585 --> 01:08:14.757
If you guys can't help me,
you gotta end it, okay?

01:08:17.051 --> 01:08:19.637
Ollie's got that gun, right?

01:08:21.389 --> 01:08:23.433
- Right?
- No, no way.

01:08:23.516 --> 01:08:26.186
You can't fuck with me on this, bro.

01:08:26.269 --> 01:08:28.062
Not with me like this.

01:08:28.146 --> 01:08:29.355
I'll do it.

01:08:30.481 --> 01:08:32.233
Just give me the gun!

01:08:34.319 --> 01:08:37.405
- We're not there yet, okay?
- Please!

01:08:37.488 --> 01:08:38.656
Joe, listen.

01:08:39.949 --> 01:08:40.992
Pal.

01:08:42.118 --> 01:08:43.369
We're gonna work something out.

01:08:43.453 --> 01:08:45.163
I just need you to hang in
a little longer, okay?

01:08:45.246 --> 01:08:46.581
Can you do that?

01:08:50.210 --> 01:08:52.921
Stay with him. I'll be back.

01:08:55.298 --> 01:08:59.761
Hattie, I need to go to the bathroom.
Will you watch Billy?

01:09:01.304 --> 01:09:02.388
Hattie?

01:09:19.447 --> 01:09:20.615
See anything?

01:09:21.324 --> 01:09:24.202
The last of those bugs
went away about four.

01:09:24.285 --> 01:09:25.370
Dawn's coming.

01:09:26.371 --> 01:09:27.747
What's on your mind?

01:09:27.830 --> 01:09:28.873
It's Joe.

01:09:30.625 --> 01:09:32.585
If we don't get him
on some serious antibiotics

01:09:32.669 --> 01:09:33.836
he's gonna die of infection.

01:09:33.920 --> 01:09:36.005
Plus he needs painkillers
in the worst way.

01:09:36.089 --> 01:09:39.842
All we've got here is liquor and aspirin.

01:09:39.926 --> 01:09:42.720
You thinking about going
to the pharmacy next door?

01:09:42.804 --> 01:09:44.681
Irene Reppler says they've got Silvadene.

01:09:44.764 --> 01:09:46.683
You know, the stuff
they use in burn wards.

01:09:46.766 --> 01:09:48.977
- She knows where they keep it.
- Slow down.

01:09:49.060 --> 01:09:50.812
You can't actually be
thinking of doing this.

01:09:50.895 --> 01:09:52.563
I'm also thinking beyond that.

01:09:52.647 --> 01:09:54.691
We have to get out of here.

01:09:55.400 --> 01:09:56.442
I mean, permanently.

01:09:56.526 --> 01:09:58.903
Why? We've got plenty to eat.

01:09:58.987 --> 01:10:02.156
And what happens when one of those things
decides to break through this window?

01:10:02.240 --> 01:10:04.909
I'm talking one of the big ones,
like the one that killed Norm.

01:10:04.993 --> 01:10:07.870
Yeah, then the flaming torch idea
didn't work so well, did it?

01:10:07.954 --> 01:10:10.373
We almost burned the goddamn store down.

01:10:16.045 --> 01:10:17.213
It's Hattie.

01:10:24.178 --> 01:10:25.596
Here?

01:10:25.680 --> 01:10:27.557
Gently now, gently.

01:10:27.640 --> 01:10:29.726
One, two, three!

01:10:39.235 --> 01:10:41.529
I don't know how long
she was there like that,

01:10:41.612 --> 01:10:43.364
lying there next to us.

01:10:43.448 --> 01:10:45.992
I thought she was sleeping.

01:10:46.075 --> 01:10:48.036
I got my 4-wheel drive.

01:10:48.119 --> 01:10:49.787
It's out there.

01:10:49.871 --> 01:10:52.332
You're talking about leaving?

01:10:52.415 --> 01:10:55.626
Well, we should hit the pharmacy first.

01:10:56.210 --> 01:10:57.712
We gotta bring back supplies
for the injured.

01:10:57.795 --> 01:11:00.006
I mean, if we don't,
Joe Eagleton's gonna die,

01:11:00.089 --> 01:11:01.758
and we can't let that happen.

01:11:02.258 --> 01:11:03.343
But after that...

01:11:04.135 --> 01:11:05.762
Look, my Land Cruiser
can hold eight people.

01:11:05.845 --> 01:11:08.056
I say we drive south
as far as the fuel takes us

01:11:08.139 --> 01:11:10.433
and try to keep clear of this mist.

01:11:10.516 --> 01:11:12.435
That's it?

01:11:12.518 --> 01:11:14.812
- That's the plan?
- That's what I got.

01:11:14.896 --> 01:11:16.147
No, you can't mean it.

01:11:16.230 --> 01:11:17.940
Not after what happened
to Norton and his group.

01:11:18.024 --> 01:11:20.401
No, no, no. Amanda, think.

01:11:20.485 --> 01:11:22.820
Norton got over 200 feet from this store,

01:11:22.904 --> 01:11:24.280
that's how much rope played out.

01:11:24.364 --> 01:11:27.158
I'm parked half that distance from here.

01:11:27.241 --> 01:11:28.701
But who knows how far
this mist has spread.

01:11:28.785 --> 01:11:30.203
It could be the entire eastern seaboard.

01:11:30.286 --> 01:11:32.830
Yeah, it could be the whole world
for all we know.

01:11:32.914 --> 01:11:35.917
Wouldn't make us any less dead,
now would it?

01:11:36.000 --> 01:11:38.836
We have one gun, how many rounds?

01:11:38.920 --> 01:11:41.130
- We got ten left.
- Ten rounds, Jesus.

01:11:41.214 --> 01:11:42.965
Okay, so ten.

01:11:43.674 --> 01:11:45.676
Want another reason
to get the hell outta here?

01:11:45.760 --> 01:11:47.929
I'll give you the best one.

01:11:48.012 --> 01:11:49.055
Her.

01:11:50.014 --> 01:11:51.724
Mrs. Carmody.

01:11:51.808 --> 01:11:54.560
She's our very own Jim Jones.

01:11:54.644 --> 01:11:57.271
I'd like to leave before people start
drinking the Kool-Aid.

01:11:57.355 --> 01:11:58.606
He's right.

01:11:58.689 --> 01:12:00.691
The flakier people get,
the better she's gonna look.

01:12:00.775 --> 01:12:03.361
No, I don't buy that.
It's obvious she's nuts.

01:12:03.444 --> 01:12:05.071
Look, a few people, maybe. But--

01:12:05.154 --> 01:12:07.281
Now I count four.
She's preaching to 'em right now.

01:12:07.365 --> 01:12:09.033
By noon, she'll have four more.

01:12:09.117 --> 01:12:11.619
By tomorrow night,
when those things come back,

01:12:11.702 --> 01:12:12.954
she'll have a congregation,

01:12:13.037 --> 01:12:15.081
and then we can start worrying about

01:12:15.164 --> 01:12:17.917
who she's gonna sacrifice
to make it all better.

01:12:19.794 --> 01:12:21.045
You, Amanda?

01:12:21.796 --> 01:12:23.047
My little boy?

01:12:23.131 --> 01:12:24.757
He's right.

01:12:24.841 --> 01:12:28.136
You don't have much faith in humanity,
do you?

01:12:28.219 --> 01:12:29.345
None whatsoever.

01:12:29.429 --> 01:12:30.805
I can't accept that.

01:12:30.888 --> 01:12:33.683
People are basically good, decent.

01:12:33.766 --> 01:12:35.977
My God, David, we're a civilized society.

01:12:36.060 --> 01:12:38.980
Sure, as long as the machines are working
and you can dial 9-1 -1.

01:12:39.063 --> 01:12:41.816
But you take those things away,
you throw people in the dark,

01:12:41.899 --> 01:12:45.778
you scare the shit outta them,
no more rules.

01:12:45.862 --> 01:12:47.697
You'll see how primitive they get.

01:12:47.780 --> 01:12:50.408
If you scare people badly enough,

01:12:50.491 --> 01:12:53.119
you can get 'em to do anything.

01:12:53.202 --> 01:12:57.123
They'll turn to whoever promises
a solution.

01:12:57.206 --> 01:12:58.207
Or whatever.

01:12:58.291 --> 01:13:00.251
Ollie, please, back me up here?

01:13:00.334 --> 01:13:02.003
I wish I could.

01:13:02.086 --> 01:13:05.339
As a species, we're fundamentally insane.

01:13:05.423 --> 01:13:06.924
Put more than two of us in a room,

01:13:07.008 --> 01:13:10.303
we pick sides and start dreaming up
reasons to kill one another.

01:13:11.429 --> 01:13:13.973
Why'd you think we invented
politics and religion?

01:13:14.056 --> 01:13:16.642
Jesus, that's just wrong.

01:13:17.643 --> 01:13:20.438
Look, nobody has to
decide anything now, okay?

01:13:20.521 --> 01:13:23.274
First things first, the pharmacy.

01:13:24.817 --> 01:13:26.527
That'll be our test run.

01:13:26.611 --> 01:13:27.653
Okay?

01:13:37.914 --> 01:13:39.874
It's all right, Big Bill.

01:13:39.957 --> 01:13:41.375
I'll bring you back some comic books.

01:13:41.459 --> 01:13:42.835
I don't want them.

01:13:42.919 --> 01:13:45.379
I want you to stay here.

01:13:45.463 --> 01:13:47.507
I won't be gone long.

01:13:47.590 --> 01:13:49.258
It's just next door.

01:13:50.760 --> 01:13:52.011
You'll be safe.

01:13:53.346 --> 01:13:56.682
Daddy, Daddy, there are things out there.

01:13:56.766 --> 01:13:57.892
Things...

01:13:58.726 --> 01:13:59.852
Yeah.

01:13:59.936 --> 01:14:02.980
There's a lot less of them in the daytime.

01:14:03.064 --> 01:14:04.273
They'll wait.

01:14:04.357 --> 01:14:05.983
They'll wait in the mist
where you can't see them,

01:14:06.067 --> 01:14:08.611
and then when you go
and can't get back in,

01:14:08.694 --> 01:14:10.112
they'll come and eat you up!

01:14:11.197 --> 01:14:12.698
Daddy, don't go!

01:14:21.749 --> 01:14:23.000
I'll be back.

01:14:24.335 --> 01:14:26.003
Big Bill, I promise.

01:14:27.421 --> 01:14:30.174
I'll be back and then
I'm gonna get you home.

01:14:30.258 --> 01:14:31.342
All right?

01:14:31.926 --> 01:14:34.178
Together, we're going home.

01:14:35.513 --> 01:14:38.432
If something happens, anything at all,
you cut and run.

01:14:38.516 --> 01:14:41.269
You get your ass back in here,
for your boy's sake.

01:14:41.352 --> 01:14:42.687
If something happens to me,

01:14:42.770 --> 01:14:45.731
I want you to take care of Billy
as best as you can,

01:14:46.232 --> 01:14:47.608
as long as you can.

01:14:47.692 --> 01:14:49.944
The Land Cruiser is yours now.

01:14:50.736 --> 01:14:53.489
You get him out of here,
you just keep driving.

01:15:00.079 --> 01:15:02.373
Where do you think you're going,
Mr. David Drayton?

01:15:02.456 --> 01:15:05.167
Are you so anxious
to make your boy an orphan?

01:15:05.251 --> 01:15:07.503
My boy is no concern of yours.

01:15:07.587 --> 01:15:08.671
Listen up.

01:15:09.338 --> 01:15:11.173
We're going to the pharmacy.

01:15:11.257 --> 01:15:12.925
We're gonna bring back some supplies.

01:15:13.009 --> 01:15:17.179
Also, there may be people trapped
over there who need help.

01:15:17.263 --> 01:15:18.472
Folks, listen!

01:15:18.556 --> 01:15:20.516
We're not gonna take any chances.

01:15:20.600 --> 01:15:24.020
If there's any trouble, we'll come
straight back here to the supermarket.

01:15:24.103 --> 01:15:27.815
And bring the fiends of hell
down on our heads, thank you.

01:15:27.898 --> 01:15:29.400
She's right.

01:15:29.483 --> 01:15:31.110
You'll make them notice us.

01:15:31.193 --> 01:15:33.154
You'll make them come.

01:15:33.237 --> 01:15:35.948
Why can't you just
leave well enough alone?

01:15:36.032 --> 01:15:37.867
Lady, is this what you call well enough?

01:15:37.950 --> 01:15:40.995
You want to stop us,
you better explain to Bobby here

01:15:41.078 --> 01:15:43.331
why we're not bringing painkillers
and medicine back for his brother.

01:15:43.414 --> 01:15:46.083
No, I'm going. Even if I have to go alone.

01:15:46.167 --> 01:15:47.877
You'll die out there, young man.

01:15:47.960 --> 01:15:50.338
You'll walk out that door
and be torn to shreds,

01:15:50.421 --> 01:15:53.758
and then your hell-bound pride
will have them come get the rest of us.

01:15:53.841 --> 01:15:56.927
Yes, they'll come back for all of us,
just like this good lady said.

01:15:57.011 --> 01:15:59.555
- Do you want that to happen, people?
- No!

01:15:59.639 --> 01:16:02.058
No, no, no!

01:16:02.141 --> 01:16:04.310
Well, it is this kind of hubris

01:16:04.393 --> 01:16:06.604
that brought the wrath of God
in the first place.

01:16:06.687 --> 01:16:08.898
This kind of pride and defiance of the--

01:16:09.649 --> 01:16:11.817
Shut up, you miserable buzzard!

01:16:11.901 --> 01:16:12.985
You old bitch!

01:16:13.069 --> 01:16:15.154
No, no, no, no, no!

01:16:16.947 --> 01:16:20.409
Stoning people who piss you off
is perfectly okay.

01:16:20.493 --> 01:16:22.453
They do it in the Bible, don't they?

01:16:22.536 --> 01:16:23.829
And I got lots of peas.

01:16:23.913 --> 01:16:26.707
David, please, if you want to go,
now's the time.

01:16:26.791 --> 01:16:28.292
How about it, Army?

01:16:28.376 --> 01:16:30.252
Any help from the armed forces?

01:16:30.336 --> 01:16:31.379
I'll go.

01:16:33.589 --> 01:16:35.174
Jim Grondin.

01:16:35.257 --> 01:16:36.759
I had you in school, didn't I?

01:16:36.842 --> 01:16:38.678
Yes, me and my sister pauline.

01:16:38.761 --> 01:16:40.638
A pair of underachievers.

01:16:40.721 --> 01:16:41.722
After you, Jim.

01:16:42.890 --> 01:16:44.475
Yes, ma'am.

01:16:44.558 --> 01:16:45.601
Shit.

01:16:45.685 --> 01:16:48.396
Is that it? That's everybody?

01:16:48.479 --> 01:16:49.730
Everybody that's going?

01:16:49.814 --> 01:16:50.898
Yes.

01:16:50.981 --> 01:16:55.194
Okay. Single file, one by one, all right?

01:16:55.277 --> 01:16:57.738
Let's get this thing over with.

01:16:57.822 --> 01:16:59.031
Let's go.

01:16:59.115 --> 01:17:00.950
- After you.
- Yes.

01:17:03.744 --> 01:17:04.745
Stay together.

01:17:09.834 --> 01:17:11.335
- Mrs. Carmody, you're not helping.
- I don't care.

01:17:11.419 --> 01:17:13.087
- Shut the hell up!
- You shut up!

01:17:20.094 --> 01:17:22.513
Save the batteries.

01:18:08.768 --> 01:18:09.852
Shit.

01:18:10.478 --> 01:18:13.647
They left the doors propped open.

01:18:13.731 --> 01:18:15.691
Think something got in?

01:18:16.901 --> 01:18:21.238
Let's just get what we need,
get the hell outta here.

01:18:21.322 --> 01:18:22.823
Yeah, let's do that.

01:18:22.907 --> 01:18:27.286
The meds are over at the end there,
in the cubicle.

01:18:47.932 --> 01:18:49.183
Will you not do that?

01:18:49.266 --> 01:18:51.143
I'm sorry. I'm sorry!

01:18:52.102 --> 01:18:53.103
God.

01:19:17.920 --> 01:19:19.088
Where's that Silvadene?

01:19:19.171 --> 01:19:20.923
It's over behind David.

01:19:21.006 --> 01:19:23.259
In the fridge, check there.

01:19:28.681 --> 01:19:31.267
- Silvadene, got it.
- Good.

01:19:31.350 --> 01:19:32.810
Ollie, what are we looking for?

01:19:32.893 --> 01:19:34.812
- Penicillin.
- Yeah.

01:19:34.895 --> 01:19:37.815
Any strong antibiotics.

01:19:37.898 --> 01:19:40.651
Pain meds, Vicodin or OxyContin.

01:19:42.111 --> 01:19:43.153
OxyContin.

01:19:44.572 --> 01:19:45.906
Hydrochloride?

01:19:48.909 --> 01:19:49.910
Penicillin.

01:20:01.714 --> 01:20:02.715
Guys...

01:20:06.010 --> 01:20:07.636
Hurry it up, I hear something.

01:20:11.891 --> 01:20:13.100
What?

01:20:14.935 --> 01:20:17.104
Something fuckin' weird.

01:20:26.113 --> 01:20:27.239
Oh, God.

01:20:27.907 --> 01:20:29.241
Oh, God.

01:20:29.325 --> 01:20:30.409
No.

01:20:31.577 --> 01:20:32.870
Oh, no.

01:20:33.579 --> 01:20:34.788
Oh, no!

01:20:34.872 --> 01:20:36.290
Aw, fuck!

01:20:38.834 --> 01:20:40.210
Look, there's another one.

01:20:40.294 --> 01:20:41.754
Oh, my God.

01:20:41.837 --> 01:20:42.922
No, no, no.

01:20:43.881 --> 01:20:45.883
Oh, no, no!

01:20:45.966 --> 01:20:49.595
Guys, let's get out of here, now.

01:20:52.181 --> 01:20:53.182
Holy shit!

01:20:59.605 --> 01:21:00.606
I'm sorry.

01:21:01.815 --> 01:21:04.193
I'm sorry. Help me!

01:21:12.076 --> 01:21:13.077
Son of a bitch!

01:21:13.160 --> 01:21:15.204
This stuff ain't coming off.

01:21:15.287 --> 01:21:16.288
Aw, man.

01:21:16.372 --> 01:21:18.123
- He's glued to this fuckin' post.
- Hang in there.

01:21:18.207 --> 01:21:20.209
It's our fault.

01:21:20.292 --> 01:21:22.252
It's all our fault.

01:21:22.336 --> 01:21:24.338
It's really stuck.

01:21:28.759 --> 01:21:31.845
I can feel them.

01:21:34.932 --> 01:21:36.308
Jesus.

01:21:43.065 --> 01:21:44.066
Oh, my God.

01:21:44.900 --> 01:21:46.402
Oh, I...

01:21:57.287 --> 01:21:58.539
There's more!

01:22:08.340 --> 01:22:10.175
There's another one! Hit it!

01:22:13.178 --> 01:22:14.638
Ollie, Ollie!

01:22:14.722 --> 01:22:17.349
- One over there.
- Ollie, Ollie, there.

01:22:18.726 --> 01:22:20.019
There, there.

01:22:20.102 --> 01:22:21.228
Shoot, shoot!

01:22:22.479 --> 01:22:23.731
Shit.

01:22:27.484 --> 01:22:29.069
Where the hell are they?

01:22:30.237 --> 01:22:31.947
Bobby!

01:22:38.704 --> 01:22:39.747
Bobby, hold on!

01:22:39.830 --> 01:22:41.206
Hold on!

01:22:41.290 --> 01:22:42.416
Cut the strand!

01:22:42.499 --> 01:22:43.792
Help me!

01:22:48.589 --> 01:22:50.299
A belt! Who's got a belt?

01:22:50.382 --> 01:22:52.885
I've got a belt!

01:22:55.804 --> 01:22:57.473
- I got him, I got him.
- Hold on!

01:23:10.611 --> 01:23:12.988
Light. Light!

01:23:19.745 --> 01:23:22.456
Come on, come on!

01:23:22.539 --> 01:23:25.751
Let's go, let's go, let's go,
let's go, let's go!

01:23:25.834 --> 01:23:27.795
Watch it, watch it!

01:23:40.682 --> 01:23:42.810
All right, go, go, go, go, go, go!

01:23:42.893 --> 01:23:45.104
Come on!

01:23:53.529 --> 01:23:54.530
Jim, go!

01:23:56.031 --> 01:23:57.658
Ollie!

01:24:02.246 --> 01:24:03.831
Kill it, kill it!

01:24:14.591 --> 01:24:16.343
- Fuckers.
- Oh, no.

01:24:16.426 --> 01:24:18.220
- God, he's dead, he's dead!
- Get outta here!

01:24:18.303 --> 01:24:19.930
Come on, let's go, let's go!

01:24:20.013 --> 01:24:22.015
Come on, come on, come on!

01:24:22.099 --> 01:24:23.183
Come on, Drayton, he's dead!

01:24:23.267 --> 01:24:24.685
Come on!

01:24:55.507 --> 01:24:58.427
Open the door!

01:24:58.510 --> 01:25:00.012
Where's Bobby?

01:25:00.095 --> 01:25:01.096
Daddy!

01:25:02.639 --> 01:25:04.766
Come on, come on, hurry up!

01:25:04.850 --> 01:25:06.351
What happened?

01:25:06.435 --> 01:25:07.436
They're dead!

01:25:07.519 --> 01:25:08.896
They're all dead!

01:25:11.106 --> 01:25:12.232
Look at him!

01:25:25.162 --> 01:25:27.122
Expiation, because we have seen

01:25:27.206 --> 01:25:30.334
that the earth is scourged
with whips and scorpions.

01:25:30.417 --> 01:25:34.254
We have seen the earth
vomit forth from her lips

01:25:34.338 --> 01:25:38.926
obscenities and profanities
of such nightmare proportions.

01:25:39.009 --> 01:25:42.512
And for these evil, lurking spirits

01:25:42.596 --> 01:25:44.848
and all these evil people with greed...

01:25:44.932 --> 01:25:46.308
How long was I out?

01:25:46.391 --> 01:25:48.101
Most of the day.

01:25:48.727 --> 01:25:51.188
You just came over here,
lied down, and went to sleep.

01:25:51.271 --> 01:25:54.524
Just passed out is more like it.

01:25:54.608 --> 01:25:56.610
I just shut down for a while.

01:25:56.693 --> 01:25:57.694
I'm sorry.

01:25:59.196 --> 01:26:00.405
Expiation!

01:26:00.489 --> 01:26:02.908
Expiation! Do you remember yesterday--

01:26:02.991 --> 01:26:04.284
How's Joe?

01:26:04.368 --> 01:26:05.535
Dead.

01:26:05.619 --> 01:26:08.747
Joe died of his burns
while you were asleep.

01:26:08.830 --> 01:26:10.499
We were just too late.

01:26:10.582 --> 01:26:12.084
I told you this was--

01:26:12.167 --> 01:26:14.461
God, I thought I was dreaming her voice.

01:26:14.544 --> 01:26:15.796
No dream.

01:26:15.879 --> 01:26:18.048
She's getting people whipped up.

01:26:18.131 --> 01:26:20.968
That poor girl is dead.

01:26:21.051 --> 01:26:23.345
And that boy is burnt in the backroom.

01:26:23.428 --> 01:26:26.765
She's got them believing she's a psychic.
She has a direct line to God.

01:26:26.848 --> 01:26:29.935
Why wouldn't they?
Woman never shuts up.

01:26:30.018 --> 01:26:33.355
Like those speeches Castro used to make.

01:26:35.691 --> 01:26:38.277
Ollie says you're thinking of leaving.

01:26:38.360 --> 01:26:39.486
I'm in.

01:26:39.569 --> 01:26:40.570
No, sorry.

01:26:41.822 --> 01:26:45.367
I mean, come on,
you saw what happened to Bobby, Mike.

01:26:45.450 --> 01:26:49.454
I won't do that again.
I won't be responsible.

01:26:49.538 --> 01:26:51.290
You might want to reconsider that.

01:26:51.373 --> 01:26:54.418
What will keep these evil,
these abominations at bay?

01:26:54.501 --> 01:26:55.877
What will keep them away?

01:26:55.961 --> 01:26:59.047
"The rock will not hide them,
the dead tree give no shelter."

01:26:59.131 --> 01:27:01.300
- What will end it, let me hear it?
- Expiation!

01:27:01.383 --> 01:27:04.261
- What are we talking about?
- Expiation!

01:27:04.344 --> 01:27:07.306
- Good, say it again like you mean it.
- Expiation!

01:27:07.389 --> 01:27:08.974
Welcome to Sesame Street.

01:27:09.057 --> 01:27:11.643
Today's word is "expiation."

01:27:11.727 --> 01:27:13.770
Hallelujah, hallelujah!

01:27:13.854 --> 01:27:17.024
That boy hasn't been right
since the pharmacy.

01:27:17.107 --> 01:27:19.401
His mind's just snapped, gone.

01:27:19.484 --> 01:27:22.029
Hasn't even been two days.

01:27:22.112 --> 01:27:24.031
Not even two days.

01:27:24.114 --> 01:27:26.366
I'm not spending the rest of my life here,
I tell you what.

01:27:26.450 --> 01:27:29.077
I can quietly gather up
some bags of groceries

01:27:29.161 --> 01:27:32.331
and hide them up
at one of the check stands by the door.

01:27:32.414 --> 01:27:34.875
It was your idea, it's your vehicle.

01:27:34.958 --> 01:27:36.460
It'll be your call.

01:27:37.919 --> 01:27:40.964
I'd rather die out there trying
than in here waiting.

01:27:43.550 --> 01:27:45.427
Who will save them? No one.

01:27:45.510 --> 01:27:47.012
The rock will not.

01:27:48.972 --> 01:27:51.433
I want some idea of what we're up against.

01:27:51.516 --> 01:27:54.269
I want to know what this mist is.

01:27:54.353 --> 01:27:55.562
I want to talk to the soldiers.

01:27:55.645 --> 01:27:57.647
Soldiers? What's that gonna do?

01:27:57.731 --> 01:27:59.524
You heard what the MP said
at the pharmacy.

01:27:59.608 --> 01:28:01.651
David, I'm not even sure
I knew he was talking.

01:28:01.735 --> 01:28:03.445
The situation was insane.

01:28:03.528 --> 01:28:07.824
He said he was sorry.
Wasn't that the word he used? Sorry?

01:28:07.908 --> 01:28:09.910
That's right.
He said it was their fault, right?

01:28:09.993 --> 01:28:11.370
What did he mean by that?

01:28:11.453 --> 01:28:13.830
That's what we're gonna find out.

01:28:13.914 --> 01:28:15.665
Irene, stay with Billy, please.

01:28:15.749 --> 01:28:16.917
Verse 17!

01:28:17.000 --> 01:28:19.503
"Poured out his vial into the air,

01:28:19.586 --> 01:28:21.421
and there came a great voice

01:28:21.505 --> 01:28:24.674
out of the temple of heaven
from the throne saying,

01:28:24.758 --> 01:28:26.927
it is done, it is done!

01:28:27.010 --> 01:28:30.722
And there were voices
and lighting and thunders

01:28:30.806 --> 01:28:33.225
and a great earthquake,
yet as we've not seen."

01:28:33.308 --> 01:28:34.976
Yes, come to me!

01:28:36.019 --> 01:28:37.437
What?

01:28:37.521 --> 01:28:38.522
Where's your friends?

01:28:38.605 --> 01:28:39.773
I ain't seen 'em.

01:28:39.856 --> 01:28:41.358
Not that big a store.
It's kinda hard to lose.

01:28:41.441 --> 01:28:43.568
I ain't seen 'em, I said.

01:28:43.652 --> 01:28:45.195
Do I look like their keeper?

01:28:48.031 --> 01:28:49.408
What do you want from me?

01:28:49.491 --> 01:28:51.243
What do you know about this mist?

01:28:51.326 --> 01:28:53.578
I don't know nothin'.
I got nothin' to do with it.

01:28:53.662 --> 01:28:55.622
That's not what the MP said
in the pharmacy

01:28:55.705 --> 01:28:57.833
before the spiders came out of his skin.

01:28:58.708 --> 01:29:00.836
They're not in the store.

01:29:00.919 --> 01:29:03.839
The only place we haven't looked
is the loading dock.

01:29:03.922 --> 01:29:07.342
Because you know,
you saw the good face of God tonight.

01:29:07.426 --> 01:29:08.969
Yes? Tell us.

01:29:09.052 --> 01:29:12.973
Here's an old man who has seen.
Yes, he has seen!

01:29:14.433 --> 01:29:17.853
And I want to save you,
I want to walk with you

01:29:17.936 --> 01:29:19.479
into my father's hands.

01:29:21.273 --> 01:29:22.274
Morales.

01:29:23.442 --> 01:29:24.484
Donaldson.

01:29:27.154 --> 01:29:28.280
Guys?

01:29:30.198 --> 01:29:32.492
It's the only place they can be.

01:29:32.576 --> 01:29:33.743
What?

01:29:33.827 --> 01:29:35.162
Couldn't just disappear.

01:29:35.245 --> 01:29:38.373
Look, I told you, okay?
I don't know where they are and I don't...

01:29:45.297 --> 01:29:47.466
I didn't think they'd do it.

01:29:47.549 --> 01:29:48.717
They said they would do it,

01:29:48.800 --> 01:29:51.928
and I told them what the Mp said
at the pharmacy,

01:29:52.012 --> 01:29:54.514
and they swore they'd do it,
I just didn't think they would.

01:29:54.598 --> 01:29:55.682
Oh, Jesus.

01:29:55.765 --> 01:29:58.810
It's the Arrowhead project, isn't it?

01:29:58.894 --> 01:30:00.020
This mist.

01:30:00.103 --> 01:30:02.647
It's some kind of what, military fuck up?

01:30:02.731 --> 01:30:04.816
What were you guys
messing with up there, huh?

01:30:04.900 --> 01:30:07.277
We got you now, you sorry son of a bitch!

01:30:07.360 --> 01:30:09.112
Get in there! It was them!

01:30:09.196 --> 01:30:11.406
It was them what done it to us!

01:30:11.490 --> 01:30:14.993
It was them what brung down
the final wrath upon us!

01:30:15.076 --> 01:30:17.537
Those two peckerwoods
that he's been with this whole time,

01:30:17.621 --> 01:30:19.831
they hung themselves
in the back because they knew.

01:30:19.915 --> 01:30:21.333
They knew it all along.

01:30:21.416 --> 01:30:22.751
No, he's crazy.
He doesn't know what he's--

01:30:22.834 --> 01:30:24.836
- Get on your knees!
- Stay out of it, Drayton.

01:30:24.920 --> 01:30:26.963
They heard it too, didn't ya? All of ya!

01:30:27.047 --> 01:30:28.340
All about the Arrowhead Project

01:30:28.423 --> 01:30:30.383
and all that secret shit
up on the mountain.

01:30:30.467 --> 01:30:32.052
That's what brung it down on us.

01:30:32.135 --> 01:30:35.514
That's what brung down the wrath of God.

01:30:37.098 --> 01:30:38.517
Private Jessup.

01:30:40.894 --> 01:30:42.896
It wasn't me.

01:30:42.979 --> 01:30:46.024
I'm stationed out there.
I'm not responsible.

01:30:46.107 --> 01:30:48.068
- Bullshit.
- Hell, I'm a local!

01:30:48.151 --> 01:30:49.819
Most of you people know me.

01:30:49.903 --> 01:30:50.904
You!

01:30:50.987 --> 01:30:54.991
Stop your chickenshit whining
or I will cut your puling tongue out.

01:30:55.075 --> 01:30:56.701
Now you tell us!

01:30:58.787 --> 01:31:00.372
Tell us.

01:31:00.455 --> 01:31:02.999
Look, look, okay, okay.

01:31:03.083 --> 01:31:04.209
I heard stuff.

01:31:04.292 --> 01:31:05.335
"Stuff."

01:31:05.418 --> 01:31:07.587
Yes, we all heard stuff.

01:31:09.005 --> 01:31:14.636
Like, how they thought
that there were other dimensions.

01:31:15.303 --> 01:31:18.014
Other worlds all around us

01:31:18.098 --> 01:31:22.102
and how they wanted
to try and make a window.

01:31:22.185 --> 01:31:25.146
You know, so they could look through
and see what's on the other side.

01:31:26.731 --> 01:31:29.526
Well, maybe your window
turned out to be a door, didn't it?

01:31:29.609 --> 01:31:31.319
Not mine, those scientists!

01:31:31.403 --> 01:31:34.656
- The scientists.
- Yes, the scientists, it wasn't me.

01:31:34.739 --> 01:31:36.366
They must've ripped a hole open
by accident,

01:31:36.449 --> 01:31:38.827
this other world came
spilling through to ours.

01:31:38.910 --> 01:31:42.038
That's what Donaldson was saying to me
right before he killed himself,

01:31:42.122 --> 01:31:43.873
I didn't understand the half of it.

01:31:45.709 --> 01:31:47.085
It ain't my fault!

01:31:49.087 --> 01:31:52.632
Ain't his fault.

01:31:53.592 --> 01:31:54.634
No, no, no.

01:31:55.594 --> 01:31:58.513
Ain't nothing ever anybody's fault.

01:31:59.598 --> 01:32:01.016
But he denies it.

01:32:02.142 --> 01:32:04.394
He points the finger.

01:32:04.477 --> 01:32:06.021
This Judas in our midst.

01:32:07.564 --> 01:32:08.940
Judas!

01:32:09.024 --> 01:32:10.442
David!

01:32:10.525 --> 01:32:12.235
You, you!

01:32:12.861 --> 01:32:14.779
Don't you know by now?

01:32:14.863 --> 01:32:16.948
Don't you know the truth?

01:32:17.032 --> 01:32:20.160
We are being punished. For what?

01:32:20.243 --> 01:32:23.246
For going against the will of God.

01:32:23.330 --> 01:32:27.792
For going against
his forbidden rules of old.

01:32:27.876 --> 01:32:29.294
Walking on the moon.

01:32:29.377 --> 01:32:30.795
Yes, yes!

01:32:30.879 --> 01:32:32.672
Or splitting his atoms.

01:32:34.883 --> 01:32:37.218
Or stem cells and abortions!

01:32:39.095 --> 01:32:41.181
And destroying the secrets of life

01:32:41.264 --> 01:32:44.309
that only God above has any right to!

01:32:44.392 --> 01:32:46.519
Amen!

01:32:46.603 --> 01:32:47.896
Yes, I know.

01:32:47.979 --> 01:32:49.606
It is true!

01:32:49.689 --> 01:32:51.900
And now we are being punished,

01:32:51.983 --> 01:32:54.527
the judgment is being
brought down upon us.

01:32:54.611 --> 01:32:57.739
The fiends of hell,
you see they are let loose.

01:32:57.822 --> 01:32:59.866
And star Wormwood blazes.

01:33:01.242 --> 01:33:04.079
- And it is his fault, yes his--
- No, no!

01:33:04.162 --> 01:33:05.955
It is not my fault!

01:33:06.039 --> 01:33:09.000
They did it!
They spit in the eye of the almighty!

01:33:09.584 --> 01:33:10.585
No!

01:33:11.586 --> 01:33:12.921
Get over there!

01:33:13.505 --> 01:33:15.173
- No!
- Judas!

01:33:19.135 --> 01:33:20.637
String him up!

01:33:23.640 --> 01:33:25.266
Stand up, you coward!

01:33:30.563 --> 01:33:31.731
Jesus!

01:33:39.989 --> 01:33:41.199
- No!
- Stop him!

01:33:44.786 --> 01:33:47.414
Feed him to the beast!

01:33:47.497 --> 01:33:48.915
Expiation!

01:33:48.998 --> 01:33:52.252
Let the abominations smell his blood!

01:33:54.462 --> 01:33:55.463
No!

01:33:58.883 --> 01:34:01.010
Jesus, wait! David!

01:34:59.152 --> 01:35:00.153
Please.

01:35:10.872 --> 01:35:14.209
The beast will leave us alone tonight.

01:35:15.335 --> 01:35:16.419
Tomorrow...

01:35:17.462 --> 01:35:20.882
Tomorrow, we'll just have to wait and see.

01:35:29.265 --> 01:35:30.266
Daddy?

01:35:32.143 --> 01:35:33.186
Daddy?

01:35:45.073 --> 01:35:47.408
I'm sorry I left you, pal.

01:35:49.285 --> 01:35:51.162
I won't ever leave you again.

01:35:52.497 --> 01:35:53.498
Promise?

01:35:55.375 --> 01:35:58.545
You have to give me
your best promise, okay?

01:35:58.628 --> 01:36:00.755
Your very best promise.

01:36:00.839 --> 01:36:02.173
You can never break it.

01:36:02.257 --> 01:36:03.258
Tell me.

01:36:05.468 --> 01:36:08.096
Promise you won't let the monsters get me.

01:36:11.516 --> 01:36:13.643
Ever, no matter what.

01:36:15.603 --> 01:36:16.604
I promise.

01:36:20.191 --> 01:36:21.943
I love you, Daddy.

01:36:22.735 --> 01:36:24.362
I love you, Billy.

01:36:24.863 --> 01:36:26.447
More than anything.

01:36:55.935 --> 01:36:56.936
It's dawn.

01:37:02.483 --> 01:37:03.651
Hey, pal.

01:37:03.735 --> 01:37:05.570
You ready to go home?

01:37:06.112 --> 01:37:07.280
Come on.

01:37:09.032 --> 01:37:10.408
Okay.

01:37:10.491 --> 01:37:12.368
I've got the groceries hidden
at check stand number 2.

01:37:12.452 --> 01:37:15.330
Five bags. We can grab 'em
and get out the door.

01:37:15.413 --> 01:37:16.706
Okay.

01:37:16.789 --> 01:37:19.959
My car's parked in the center lane
of the parking lot, far end.

01:37:20.043 --> 01:37:22.712
Whoever gets there first
open up both doors,

01:37:22.795 --> 01:37:24.964
and we'll all pile in
as fast as we can, okay?

01:37:25.048 --> 01:37:26.049
Let's go.

01:37:49.697 --> 01:37:51.366
Stealing food now?

01:37:56.454 --> 01:37:59.290
Going out now, Mrs. Carmody.

01:37:59.374 --> 01:38:01.876
Please stand aside.

01:38:01.960 --> 01:38:05.004
You can't go out, I won't allow it.

01:38:05.088 --> 01:38:06.089
Won't allow it?

01:38:06.172 --> 01:38:09.008
It's against God's will.

01:38:09.092 --> 01:38:11.344
Don't you know that by now?

01:38:11.427 --> 01:38:16.432
Haven't I proven myself
again and again and again?

01:38:16.516 --> 01:38:19.602
Haven't I shown that I am his vessel?

01:38:24.899 --> 01:38:27.735
What's the matter with you?

01:38:29.737 --> 01:38:32.115
Don't you believe in God?

01:38:32.198 --> 01:38:34.784
No one's interfered with you,

01:38:34.867 --> 01:38:36.911
all we're asking for
is the same privilege.

01:38:36.995 --> 01:38:37.996
You heard him.

01:38:39.998 --> 01:38:43.668
It is these people
who brought this upon us.

01:38:45.294 --> 01:38:50.174
They, people who refuse
to bend to the will of God

01:38:50.258 --> 01:38:52.427
and claim it privilege.

01:38:53.052 --> 01:38:55.638
Sinners in pride.

01:38:56.305 --> 01:38:58.266
Yes, haughty.

01:38:58.349 --> 01:38:59.517
Privileged!

01:39:00.226 --> 01:39:05.773
They mock us, they mock our god,
our faith, our values,

01:39:05.857 --> 01:39:07.525
our very lifestyle.

01:39:07.608 --> 01:39:10.945
They mock our humility and our piousness.

01:39:12.071 --> 01:39:14.240
They piss on us and laugh.

01:39:18.161 --> 01:39:22.540
It's from them
the blood of human sacrifice must come.

01:39:23.499 --> 01:39:24.625
From them.

01:39:26.127 --> 01:39:28.129
The blood of expiation.

01:39:29.881 --> 01:39:31.132
You try it.

01:39:31.215 --> 01:39:33.760
You fuckin' try it! Come on.

01:39:34.385 --> 01:39:36.054
We want the boy.

01:39:36.137 --> 01:39:37.513
- You get back!
- We want the boy!

01:39:37.597 --> 01:39:39.682
You get back!

01:39:42.268 --> 01:39:44.103
Grab that boy! Grab him!

01:39:48.149 --> 01:39:49.484
Grab him!

01:39:51.110 --> 01:39:52.945
And get the whore too!

01:39:53.029 --> 01:39:54.030
Grab her!

01:39:54.572 --> 01:39:55.740
Kill them!

01:39:55.823 --> 01:39:56.991
Kill them all!

01:40:12.048 --> 01:40:15.802
Stay down, stay down, stay down.

01:40:21.599 --> 01:40:22.850
I killed her.

01:40:24.852 --> 01:40:26.229
Thank you, Ollie.

01:40:27.939 --> 01:40:28.981
Let's go.

01:40:30.316 --> 01:40:32.902
Get that ice machine
out of the way, please.

01:40:35.822 --> 01:40:37.490
- You killed her!
- Come on.

01:40:37.573 --> 01:40:39.826
You murdered her!

01:40:43.538 --> 01:40:46.666
I wouldn't have shot her, Dave.
Not if there had been any other way.

01:40:46.749 --> 01:40:48.376
That's why I said thank you.

01:40:48.459 --> 01:40:49.460
Okay.

01:40:49.544 --> 01:40:51.879
Okay, then. Let's go!

01:40:53.172 --> 01:40:54.841
Get up, Myron!

01:40:54.924 --> 01:40:56.092
Come on, we gotta go!

01:40:56.175 --> 01:40:58.469
My ankle!

01:41:06.769 --> 01:41:08.354
All the way down!

01:41:09.397 --> 01:41:10.648
Where are they?

01:41:10.731 --> 01:41:12.233
Bud, Myron?

01:41:12.316 --> 01:41:13.526
Ambrose!

01:41:13.609 --> 01:41:15.319
- I think I broke it!
- Fuck.

01:41:15.403 --> 01:41:16.696
Come on, come on, come on!

01:41:16.779 --> 01:41:18.197
We gotta go, come on, come on!

01:41:18.281 --> 01:41:19.532
They're lost!

01:41:28.124 --> 01:41:30.877
- Oh, Jesus. Ollie!
- Ollie!

01:42:11.125 --> 01:42:13.878
All that screaming.

01:42:13.961 --> 01:42:16.714
Are they out there? Can they see us?

01:42:26.140 --> 01:42:28.935
Let me in!

01:42:43.074 --> 01:42:44.325
Are we going?

01:42:51.415 --> 01:42:52.416
No.

01:42:52.500 --> 01:42:54.919
- No, no, no.
- Yeah, yeah.

01:42:55.002 --> 01:42:56.379
David.

01:42:56.462 --> 01:42:58.297
- David, no.
- Daddy, no.

01:42:58.381 --> 01:42:59.715
- David!
- Daddy!

01:42:59.799 --> 01:43:01.384
Get back in the car!

01:43:01.467 --> 01:43:02.718
- Daddy!
- David!

01:43:13.604 --> 01:43:14.814
Oh, my God!

01:43:18.150 --> 01:43:19.443
Oh, my God.

01:43:39.839 --> 01:43:41.299
We gotta go.

01:45:40.543 --> 01:45:42.545
I told her I'd fix it.

01:45:46.257 --> 01:45:48.426
Front window, broken open.

01:45:52.763 --> 01:45:54.014
Tree.

01:45:56.475 --> 01:46:00.312
My grandfather's tree.

01:46:15.703 --> 01:46:18.789
I'm sorry, David. I'm just so sorry.

01:46:32.970 --> 01:46:34.180
Let's...

01:46:36.432 --> 01:46:39.435
See how far this fuel takes us, huh?

01:46:44.857 --> 01:46:47.693
Maybe we'll get clear of this mist.

01:50:03.180 --> 01:50:04.181
Well...

01:50:06.183 --> 01:50:07.935
We gave it a good shot.

01:50:08.811 --> 01:50:11.063
Nobody could say we didn't.

01:50:12.481 --> 01:50:13.649
Nope.

01:50:14.233 --> 01:50:16.318
Nobody can say that.

01:51:45.157 --> 01:51:46.325
Well...

01:51:48.327 --> 01:51:49.953
we've got...

01:51:54.458 --> 01:51:55.501
Four.

01:52:00.214 --> 01:52:01.590
Four bullets.

01:52:05.636 --> 01:52:07.221
But there's five of us.

01:52:17.606 --> 01:52:19.650
I'll figure something out.

01:53:50.157 --> 01:53:51.408
God!

01:54:18.268 --> 01:54:19.603
Come on!

01:54:25.108 --> 01:54:26.443
Come on!

01:54:28.111 --> 01:54:30.155
Come on!

01:54:33.241 --> 01:54:35.410
Come on, come on, come on.

01:54:46.672 --> 01:54:48.799
Come on, come on, come on.

01:54:52.678 --> 01:54:56.306
Come on, come on!

01:56:36.239 --> 01:56:38.950
They're dead, for what?
